{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyDzPfctmNZKsxsqXWU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4903,"cache_read_input_tokens":122336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4903},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"599b2018-4b29-4e52-8f4f-1ce316b5a964","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:45.935Z","request_id":"req_011CggyDyyc6epkEjykGCXRw","thinking_duration_ms":22966,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyDzPfctmNZKsxsqXWU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U6eZJRmihyCg9KPTicSYF2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; cat kits/README.md; echo ----; cat package.json; echo ----; cat index.html | head -70","description":"Read the kits table, package.json, and handoff index page"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4903,"cache_read_input_tokens":122336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4903},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"ed29f741-3efa-4009-b99f-a041e4ba9cb9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:47.041Z","request_id":"req_011CggyDyyc6epkEjykGCXRw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U6eZJRmihyCg9KPTicSYF2":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; cat kits/README.md; echo ----; cat package.json; echo ----; cat index.html | head -70","description":"Read the kits table, package.json, and handoff index page"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6eZJRmihyCg9KPTicSYF2","type":"tool_result","content":"# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n\nA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\nits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n\n- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n  its deep links and how it works.\n- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n\n**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\ngame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n\n| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n\n**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\nsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\na world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n----\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n  \"version\": \"0.85.2\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge for coding agents: the engine, its card, index and guide, the tools and a template game\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node game/test.mjs\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"\n  }\n}\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>my-3D2dge handoff package</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #1b1726; --paper: #f6f3ee; --line: #d8d2c8; --accent: #6a4ad0 }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --ink: #ece8f6; --paper: #15121c; --line: #3a3348; --accent: #a68cff } }\n  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif }\n  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 48px }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem } p { margin: .5rem 0 1rem }\n  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line) }\n  li { padding: .6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) } a { color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace }\n  li span { display: block; font-size: .9rem; opacity: .8 }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n<h1>my-3D2dge handoff package</h1>\n<p>v0.85.2 · dev-build. Everything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full engine, as text files. Start with <a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a>, then read <a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a>. Play <a href=\"kits/README.md\">a genre kit</a> or <a href=\"game/index.html\">the template game</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a><span>start here: what the package holds, which page to read, how to run and test a game</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"package.json\">package.json</a><span>pins Playwright for the tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge.js\">my-3d2dge.js</a><span>the full engine, readable: the core and every module</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge-agent.js\">my-3d2dge-agent.js</a><span>the agent edition: the essential engine, its header a short manual</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/arcade.js\">modules/arcade.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/click.js\">modules/click.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/drive.js\">modules/drive.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/fight.js\">modules/fight.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/gen.js\">modules/gen.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/grid.js\">modules/grid.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/mode7.js\">modules/mode7.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/physics.js\">modules/physics.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rhythm.js\">modules/rhythm.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/road.js\">modules/road.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rooms.js\">modules/rooms.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rpg.js\">modules/rpg.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/songs.js\">modules/songs.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/story.js\">modules/story.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/strategy.js\">modules/strategy.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/terrain.js\">modules/terrain.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a><span>the API card: read it whole</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API-INDEX.md\">API-INDEX.md</a><span>every public name, one line each: search it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"AI_GUIDE.md\">AI_GUIDE.md</a><span>the guide: recipes, the look, heights, sessions</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/check.mjs\">tools/check.mjs</a><span>plays a game headless and reports errors, screenshots and its snapshot</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/filmstrip.mjs\">tools/filmstrip.mjs</a><span>records frames into one picture</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/replay.mjs\">tools/replay.mjs</a><span>replays a recorded play session exactly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"docs/ASSETS.md\">docs/ASSETS.md</a><span>the asset card: objects and materials as data (r.shape), the core library, writing one</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-find.mjs\">tools/asset-find.mjs</a><span>searches the core library and the store: node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-sheet.mjs\">tools/asset-sheet.mjs</a><span>draws an object in every view and says what reads badly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-set.mjs\">tools/asset-set.mjs</a><span>cuts the few entries a game uses from the store's sets</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-lib.mjs\">tools/asset-lib.mjs</a><span>shared by the asset tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/game.js\">game/game.js</a><span>the template game: copy it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/index.html\">game/index.html</a><span>the template game: play it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/test.mjs\">game/test.mjs</a><span>its headless test: node game/test.mjs</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"kits/README.md\">kits/</a><span>the 22 genre kits, readable: each kit's game and the page that plays it (kits/arcade.html), the table of them, and their headless test (node kits/test.mjs)</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"src/assets/README.md\">src/assets/</a><span>the asset store: 29 sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries, and their catalogs (docs/ASSETS.md, \"Make one\")</span></li>\n</ul>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"97723611-cf69-4805-8c8c-ceeb9d5c3e3e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:47.069Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n\nA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\nits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n\n- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n  its deep links and how it works.\n- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n\n**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\ngame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n\n| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n\n**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\nsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\na world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n----\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n  \"version\": \"0.85.2\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge for coding agents: the engine, its card, index and guide, the tools and a template game\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node game/test.mjs\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"\n  }\n}\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>my-3D2dge handoff package</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #1b1726; --paper: #f6f3ee; --line: #d8d2c8; --accent: #6a4ad0 }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --ink: #ece8f6; --paper: #15121c; --line: #3a3348; --accent: #a68cff } }\n  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif }\n  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 48px }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem } p { margin: .5rem 0 1rem }\n  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line) }\n  li { padding: .6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) } a { color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace }\n  li span { display: block; font-size: .9rem; opacity: .8 }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n<h1>my-3D2dge handoff package</h1>\n<p>v0.85.2 · dev-build. Everything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full engine, as text files. Start with <a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a>, then read <a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a>. Play <a href=\"kits/README.md\">a genre kit</a> or <a href=\"game/index.html\">the template game</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a><span>start here: what the package holds, which page to read, how to run and test a game</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"package.json\">package.json</a><span>pins Playwright for the tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge.js\">my-3d2dge.js</a><span>the full engine, readable: the core and every module</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge-agent.js\">my-3d2dge-agent.js</a><span>the agent edition: the essential engine, its header a short manual</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/arcade.js\">modules/arcade.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/click.js\">modules/click.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/drive.js\">modules/drive.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/fight.js\">modules/fight.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/gen.js\">modules/gen.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/grid.js\">modules/grid.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/mode7.js\">modules/mode7.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/physics.js\">modules/physics.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rhythm.js\">modules/rhythm.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/road.js\">modules/road.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rooms.js\">modules/rooms.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rpg.js\">modules/rpg.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/songs.js\">modules/songs.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/story.js\">modules/story.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/strategy.js\">modules/strategy.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/terrain.js\">modules/terrain.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a><span>the API card: read it whole</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API-INDEX.md\">API-INDEX.md</a><span>every public name, one line each: search it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"AI_GUIDE.md\">AI_GUIDE.md</a><span>the guide: recipes, the look, heights, sessions</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/check.mjs\">tools/check.mjs</a><span>plays a game headless and reports errors, screenshots and its snapshot</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/filmstrip.mjs\">tools/filmstrip.mjs</a><span>records frames into one picture</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/replay.mjs\">tools/replay.mjs</a><span>replays a recorded play session exactly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"docs/ASSETS.md\">docs/ASSETS.md</a><span>the asset card: objects and materials as data (r.shape), the core library, writing one</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-find.mjs\">tools/asset-find.mjs</a><span>searches the core library and the store: node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-sheet.mjs\">tools/asset-sheet.mjs</a><span>draws an object in every view and says what reads badly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-set.mjs\">tools/asset-set.mjs</a><span>cuts the few entries a game uses from the store's sets</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-lib.mjs\">tools/asset-lib.mjs</a><span>shared by the asset tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/game.js\">game/game.js</a><span>the template game: copy it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/index.html\">game/index.html</a><span>the template game: play it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/test.mjs\">game/test.mjs</a><span>its headless test: node game/test.mjs</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"kits/README.md\">kits/</a><span>the 22 genre kits, readable: each kit's game and the page that plays it (kits/arcade.html), the table of them, and their headless test (node kits/test.mjs)</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"src/assets/README.md\">src/assets/</a><span>the asset store: 29 sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries, and their catalogs (docs/ASSETS.md, \"Make one\")</span></li>\n</ul>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U6eZJRmihyCg9KPTicSYF2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
