{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyH5cXgvCR1rnh67Rzp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018e9GxBhmLaR8Niq9Cyx7E6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; grep -n \"pointer\\|padAim\\|lastDevice\\|glyph\\|symbols\\|buttonStyle\\|label(\\|rumble\\|cursor\\|hideCursor\\|lockPointer\\|pointerLock\\|mouseDown\\|Mouse0\\|Mouse2\\|feed(\" API-INDEX.md | head -50","description":"Search API index for pointer, gamepad aim, and glyph names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4394,"cache_read_input_tokens":146059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4394},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"1d39b51c-2b5b-46f4-8499-2781abc7793d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:08.668Z","request_id":"req_011CggyH5Q8Do74kRGSBLVzY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018e9GxBhmLaR8Niq9Cyx7E6":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; grep -n \"pointer\\|padAim\\|lastDevice\\|glyph\\|symbols\\|buttonStyle\\|label(\\|rumble\\|cursor\\|hideCursor\\|lockPointer\\|pointerLock\\|mouseDown\\|Mouse0\\|Mouse2\\|feed(\" API-INDEX.md | head -50","description":"Search API index for pointer, gamepad aim, and glyph names"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018e9GxBhmLaR8Niq9Cyx7E6","type":"tool_result","content":"100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n279:- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n306:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n312:- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n346:- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport); window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround) or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min) when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true, edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch; its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n851:- `level.crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3)` †: start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more; 0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1262:- `click.end()` †: the step's pointer stops changing the canvas's cursor (call on leaving the scene)\n1272:- `click.update(dt)` †: read the pointer and keys, walk the hero, run the talk and the hero's line; true while play should wait\n1279:- `click.item = null` †: the item on the cursor (or null)\n1347:- `fightselect.draw(r)` †: draw the roster, the cursors and each side's fighter large\n1348:- `fightselect.update(dt)` †: move the cursors, take the picks; onDone(ids) once both have one\n1349:- `fightselect.at` †: each side's cursor\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n1628:- `rpg.list(g, x, y, w, rows, o = {})`: a window of rows ({ label, note, icon, off }) with a cursor; o: { cursor, title, top (the first row shown), show (rows shown: 8), bg, rowH }. → { x, y, w, h, row(px, py) }: the row index at a screen point, or -1\n1679:- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\n1694:- `strategy.input(o = {})` †: the player's pointer and keys, each step (see the manual): selection, groups, orders. o.order: the action that orders (Mouse2 by default where it is bound); o.at(sx, sy) -> the world point under a screen point (map.pick's, by default)\n1719:- `E.tooltip(r, x, y, lines)` †: a box of lines (text, or [text, color]) beside a screen point (the pointer), kept on the screen\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"55155bed-02e9-47a7-beb0-14725b7865a9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:08.691Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n279:- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n306:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n312:- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n346:- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport); window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround) or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min) when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true, edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch; its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n851:- `level.crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3)` †: start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more; 0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1262:- `click.end()` †: the step's pointer stops changing the canvas's cursor (call on leaving the scene)\n1272:- `click.update(dt)` †: read the pointer and keys, walk the hero, run the talk and the hero's line; true while play should wait\n1279:- `click.item = null` †: the item on the cursor (or null)\n1347:- `fightselect.draw(r)` †: draw the roster, the cursors and each side's fighter large\n1348:- `fightselect.update(dt)` †: move the cursors, take the picks; onDone(ids) once both have one\n1349:- `fightselect.at` †: each side's cursor\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n1628:- `rpg.list(g, x, y, w, rows, o = {})`: a window of rows ({ label, note, icon, off }) with a cursor; o: { cursor, title, top (the first row shown), show (rows shown: 8), bg, rowH }. → { x, y, w, h, row(px, py) }: the row index at a screen point, or -1\n1679:- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\n1694:- `strategy.input(o = {})` †: the player's pointer and keys, each step (see the