{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0166ey7zkxGWe2qAsxWw3ZiD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Big Buck Hunter Pro arcade 2006 gameplay modes animals bonus rounds doe penalty\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Big_Buck_Hunter_Pro\"},{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-22443/\"},{\"title\":\"giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/big-buck-hunter-pro/3030-22443/\"},{\"title\":\"At a glance\",\"url\":\"https://www.macworld.com/article/1144021/bigbuckhunterreview.html\"},{\"title\":\"At a glance\",\"url\":\"https://www.macworld.com/article/201225/bigbuckhunterreview.html\"},{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter Pro opens its shooting gallery on Xbox for Windows Phone\",\"url\":\"https://windowscentral.com/big-buck-hunter-pro-opens-its-shooting-gallery-windows-phone\"},{\"title\":\"docs.google.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12T7Wst__pq-24JOm_apNPiustnKAEDtY8pDX4SgicM0/export?format=pdf\"},{\"title\":\"servermove.retailgazette.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://servermove.retailgazette.co.uk/?p=17039\"},{\"title\":\"Follow TV Tropes\",\"url\":\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/BigBuckHunter\"},{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/wii/big-buck-hunter-pro\"},{\"title\":\"Pro Staff Blog\",\"url\":\"https://huntinglife.com/?p=11942\"},{\"title\":\"Raw Thrills\",\"url\":\"https://mpamusement.com/collections/video-games/products/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-shooting-game\"},{\"title\":\"big buck hunter pro arcade machine 9210\",\"url\":\"https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-machine-9210/\"},{\"title\":\"big buck hunter pro 2 gun multiplayer edition tv game\",\"url\":\"https://www.esrb.org/ratings/26835/big-buck-hunter-pro-2-gun-multiplayer-edition-tv-game/\"},{\"title\":\"LaunchBox Logo Back to Home Page\",\"url\":\"https://gamesdb.launchbox-app.com/games/details/165628\"},{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter Pro Adventure Review: Hunting big game on Windows\",\"url\":\"https://www.windowscentral.com/big-buck-hunter-pro-adventure-windows-8-review\"},{\"title\":\"Big Buck Hunter\",\"url\":\"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Big_Buck_Hunter.html\"},{\"title\":\"Journalist Tool\",\"url\":\"https://jt.kineticist.com/items/a1046860-21bd-45b1-ac47-061f24022f91\"}]\n\nThe search turned up consistent information on the doe penalty, modes, and bonus rounds, though most sources are fan wikis, reviews, or retailer pages rather than the manufacturer.\n\n**Doe penalty:** Shooting a doe ends the round. One source says if one player shoots a doe, they are done until the next site begins. Another says shooting one makes the level end instantly, forcing you on to the next one. The ESRB rating summary describes players being penalized for killing the doe (female deer).\n\n**Targets:** Each round presents three bucks, and as the game progresses it gets more challenging. Elk also appear as targets in some treks. Critters are a bonus scoring element: you will see critters appear along with the antlered species or main hunting piece of the game, which you can now shoot for added bonus points.\n\n**Modes:** The Trek/Adventure structure is covered by one source, which says you can choose to do a single Trek or do the full Adventure. Another describes 'Bonus Only' lets players choose from any of the bonus games that come up after a trek ends. Multiplayer is described as up to 4 players can play, taking turns to shoot the most Bucks.\n\n**Bonus rounds:** Counts vary by version. One source says the cabinet has 5 animals available for hunting (6 for online cabinets), 15 bonus rounds (3 extras for online cabinets), and 12 critters to shoot. Bonus rounds appear between each area. Examples include Duck Hunt, Pheasant Hunt, Mars Needs Cattle, and Boars Gone Wild. Bonus rounds can also give extra points, such as a Double Bonus worth 2,000 pts for 100% accuracy on bonus items, per a fan wiki.\n\n**Caveats:** The sources describe different releases (arcade, Windows Phone, and later versions), so mode names and counts may not match a specific cabinet. The Windows Phone and Windows 8 pages also describe the phone version rather than the arcade cabinet.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"9da12604-3ab1-4794-9627-7e4fce9a252a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:46.989Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Big Buck Hunter Pro arcade 2006 gameplay modes animals bonus rounds doe penalty","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013eJTv475oUoy4MXRsH7Kx5","content":[{"title":"Big Buck Hunter Pro","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Big_Buck_Hunter_Pro"},{"title":"Big Buck Hunter Pro","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-22443/"},{"title":"giantbomb.com","url":"https://giantbomb.com/big-buck-hunter-pro/3030-22443/"},{"title":"At a glance","url":"https://www.macworld.com/article/1144021/bigbuckhunterreview.html"},{"title":"At a glance","url":"https://www.macworld.com/article/201225/bigbuckhunterreview.html"},{"title":"Big Buck Hunter Pro opens its shooting gallery on Xbox for Windows Phone","url":"https://windowscentral.com/big-buck-hunter-pro-opens-its-shooting-gallery-windows-phone"},{"title":"docs.google.com","url":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12T7Wst__pq-24JOm_apNPiustnKAEDtY8pDX4SgicM0/export?format=pdf"},{"title":"servermove.retailgazette.co.uk","url":"https://servermove.retailgazette.co.uk/?p=17039"},{"title":"Follow TV Tropes","url":"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/BigBuckHunter"},{"title":"Big Buck Hunter Pro","url":"https://www.mobygames.com/game/wii/big-buck-hunter-pro"},{"title":"Pro Staff Blog","url":"https://huntinglife.com/?p=11942"},{"title":"Raw Thrills","url":"https://mpamusement.com/collections/video-games/products/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-shooting-game"},{"title":"big buck hunter pro arcade machine 9210","url":"https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-machine-9210/"},{"title":"big buck hunter pro 2 gun multiplayer edition tv game","url":"https://www.esrb.org/ratings/26835/big-buck-hunter-pro-2-gun-multiplayer-edition-tv-game/"},{"title":"LaunchBox Logo Back to Home Page","url":"https://gamesdb.launchbox-app.com/games/details/165628"},{"title":"Big Buck Hunter Pro Adventure Review: Hunting big game on Windows","url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/big-buck-hunter-pro-adventure-windows-8-review"},{"title":"Big Buck Hunter","url":"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Big_Buck_Hunter.html"},{"title":"Journalist Tool","url":"https://jt.kineticist.com/items/a1046860-21bd-45b1-ac47-061f24022f91"}]},"The search turned up consistent information on the doe penalty, modes, and bonus rounds, though most sources are fan wikis, reviews, or retailer pages rather than the manufacturer.\n\n**Doe penalty:** Shooting a doe ends the round. One source says if one player shoots a doe, they are done until the next site begins. Another says shooting one makes the level end instantly, forcing you on to the next one. The ESRB rating summary describes players being penalized for killing the doe (female deer).\n\n**Targets:** Each round presents three bucks, and as the game progresses it gets more challenging. Elk also appear as targets in some treks. Critters are a bonus scoring element: you will see critters appear along with the antlered species or main hunting piece of the game, which you can now shoot for added bonus points.\n\n**Modes:** The Trek/Adventure structure is covered by one source, which says you can choose to do a single Trek or do the full Adventure. Another describes 'Bonus Only' lets players choose from any of the bonus games that come up after a trek ends. Multiplayer is described as up to 4 players can play, taking turns to shoot the most Bucks.\n\n**Bonus rounds:** Counts vary by version. One source says the cabinet has 5 animals available for hunting (6 for online cabinets), 15 bonus rounds (3 extras for online cabinets), and 12 critters to shoot. Bonus rounds appear between each area. Examples include Duck Hunt, Pheasant Hunt, Mars Needs Cattle, and Boars Gone Wild. Bonus rounds can also give extra points, such as a Double Bonus worth 2,000 pts for 100% accuracy on bonus items, per a fan wiki.\n\n**Caveats:** The sources describe different releases (arcade, Windows Phone, and later versions), so mode names and counts may not match a specific cabinet. The Windows Phone and Windows 8 pages also describe the phone version rather than the arcade cabinet."],"durationSeconds":6.521269635999983,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0166ey7zkxGWe2qAsxWw3ZiD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01REmepPHY7n294USFDyv7BR","type":"tool_result","content":"**Big Buck Hunter Pro (2006)**\n\n- **Developer:** Play Mechanix designed the game. Raw Thrills took over production and distribution under a January 2006 agreement.\n- **Publisher:** Raw Thrills, which took over from Incredible Technologies for the Pro/Safari series.\n- **Release:** Arcade on January 23, 2006. Later ports came to iOS (October 2009), Wii (September 2010), and Windows (February 2013, as *Big Buck Hunter Pro Adventure*).\n- **Cabinet:** It uses a two-gun platform, unlike the single-gun earlier series, and supports head-to-head play.\n- **Goal:** Shoot the male animals (bucks) as they run across the screen. Shooting a female means the player is out. \"If a player shoots a female animal, they are out\" is the article's wording.\n- **Structure:** The hunt is split into five screens called \"treks,\" and a bonus round ends the session. A round ends when all males are shot or when some escape.\n- **Scoring:** Points depend on distance, animal weight, and accuracy.\n- **Animals and regions:** Pro added animals and critters, and *Open Season* (2009) later added more. The article does not list the animals or hunt locations for Pro specifically.\n- **Tournaments:** Pro hosted monthly national tournaments, usually running from the 7th to the 27th of each month.\n- **Not covered:** The article doesn't describe pump-action mechanics, bonus or critter round details, trophy animals (trophy hunting belongs to *Safari*), or the tone and announcer.\n\n**Other series entries**\n\n- *Big Buck Hunter* (2000), *Shooter's Challenge* (2002), *Sportsman's Paradise* (2002), and *Call of the Wild* (2005), all from Incredible Technologies\n- *Big Buck Safari* (2008), which introduced African trophy hunting\n- *Open Season* (2009), which added animals to Pro\n- *Big Buck World* (2010), which combined *Open Season* and *Safari*\n- *Big Buck HD* (2012), *HD Wild* (2015), and *Reloaded* (2020)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"b742a818-8775-4273-86f6-e87eb7194ada","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:50.801Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":159396,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Big Buck Hunter Pro (2006)**\n\n- **Developer:** Play Mechanix designed the game. Raw Thrills took over production and distribution under a January 2006 agreement.\n- **Publisher:** Raw Thrills, which took over from Incredible Technologies for the Pro/Safari series.\n- **Release:** Arcade on January 23, 2006. Later ports came to iOS (October 2009), Wii (September 2010), and Windows (February 2013, as *Big Buck Hunter Pro Adventure*).\n- **Cabinet:** It uses a two-gun platform, unlike the single-gun earlier series, and supports head-to-head play.\n- **Goal:** Shoot the male animals (bucks) as they run across the screen. Shooting a female means the player is out. \"If a player shoots a female animal, they are out\" is the article's wording.\n- **Structure:** The hunt is split into five screens called \"treks,\" and a bonus round ends the session. A round ends when all males are shot or when some escape.\n- **Scoring:** Points depend on distance, animal weight, and accuracy.\n- **Animals and regions:** Pro added animals and critters, and *Open Season* (2009) later added more. The article does not list the animals or hunt locations for Pro specifically.\n- **Tournaments:** Pro hosted monthly national tournaments, usually running from the 7th to the 27th of each month.\n- **Not covered:** The article doesn't describe pump-action mechanics, bonus or critter round details, trophy animals (trophy hunting belongs to *Safari*), or the tone and announcer.\n\n**Other series entries**\n\n- *Big Buck Hunter* (2000), *Shooter's Challenge* (2002), *Sportsman's Paradise* (2002), and *Call of the Wild* (2005), all from Incredible Technologies\n- *Big Buck Safari* (2008), which introduced African trophy hunting\n- *Open Season* (2009), which added animals to Pro\n- *Big Buck World* (2010), which combined *Open Season* and *Safari*\n- *Big Buck HD* (2012), *HD Wild* (2015), and *Reloaded* (2020)","durationMs":8580,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Buck_Hunter"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01REmepPHY7n294USFDyv7BR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
