{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CAXBUq9vUSmGf3xR5GbtU6","type":"tool_result","content":"165:- `E.ik3(a, b, L1, L2, hint)`: two-bone IK in 3D: returns [joint, end]. hint points the way the joint should bend.\n176:- `E.ramp(c, n = 5, strength = 1)`: a ramp of n colors from dark to light around a base color (hue shifted), for palettes and gradients\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n224:- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n225:- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n230:- `view.ax`, `view.ay`: screen x = ax * x + ay * y (the projection's first row)\n231:- `view.bx`, `view.by`, `view.bz`: screen y = bx * x + by * y + bz * z (the second row; bz < 0 lifts things up the screen)\n232:- `view.dx`, `view.dy`, `view.dz`: the direction toward the camera, for true depth (view.depth)\n233:- `view.fx`, `view.fy`: the ground direction that points at the camera (the front of a wall faces it)\n234:- `view.id`: its name ('iso', or yours)\n235:- `view.inv`: the inverse of the ground projection (screen -> ground at z 0), null in side views\n236:- `view.isSide`: a side view (pitch 1 or less: x right, z up, y is depth)\n237:- `view.isTop`: looking straight down (pitch 89 or more)\n238:- `view.label`: its name for people ('Isometric')\n239:- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n240:- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n241:- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n242:- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n243:- `view.zBoost`: how much heights are stretched on screen (1 = true)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n1082:- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n1094:- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"8b4e180b-8eee-4ba9-b4ca-b8a11de68062","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:31.091Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"165:- `E.ik3(a, b, L1, L2, hint)`: two-bone IK in 3D: returns [joint, end]. hint points the way the joint should bend.\n176:- `E.ramp(c, n = 5, strength = 1)`: a ramp of n colors from dark to light around a base color (hue shifted), for palettes and gradients\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n224:- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n225:- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 