{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyUjeok3kjw9DzUVf9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AtPC2RqATx4t2fCmzDzWSL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; node -e \"\nconst c=require('./src/assets/catalogs/kenney-nature.json'); const items=c.items||c.entries||c; \nconst arr=Array.isArray(items)?items:Object.entries(items).map(([k,v])=>Object.assign({id:k},v));\nconsole.log(arr.length); console.log(arr.map(e=>e.id||e.name).join(' '));\" 2>&1 | head -30; sed -n '1,40p' docs/ASSETS.md","description":"List kenney-nature asset ids and read asset card intro"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4466,"cache_read_input_tokens":201559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4466},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"8785fe88-6149-48b2-b8e1-2c6cacc944e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:46.485Z","request_id":"req_011CggyUjRAwZ5yJ2BigbdiG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AtPC2RqATx4t2fCmzDzWSL":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff; node -e \"\nconst c=require('./src/assets/catalogs/kenney-nature.json'); const items=c.items||c.entries||c; \nconst arr=Array.isArray(items)?items:Object.entries(items).map(([k,v])=>Object.assign({id:k},v));\nconsole.log(arr.length); console.log(arr.map(e=>e.id||e.name).join(' '));\" 2>&1 | head -30; sed -n '1,40p' docs/ASSETS.md","description":"List kenney-nature asset ids and read asset card intro"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AtPC2RqATx4t2fCmzDzWSL","type":"tool_result","content":"48\n$sources $skip $mats bed bed-floor campfire-bricks crop-pumpkin crops-bamboo-stage-a fence-simple-high fence-simple-low lily-large log-large pot-large pot-small rock-small-g statue-column statue-column-damaged statue-head statue-obelisk stone-small-flat-a stone-small-g stone-small-h stone-tall-b stone-tall-c stone-tall-e stump-round stump-square-detailed tent-detailed-closed tent-small-closed tree-blocks tree-cone tree-default tree-default-dark tree-detailed tree-fat tree-fat-fall tree-oak tree-oak-fall tree-pine-default-a tree-pine-ground-a tree-pine-round-a tree-pine-round-d tree-pine-small-a tree-pine-small-c tree-pine-tall-c tree-pine-tall-d-detailed tree-small tree-tall\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"9f48990c-7a78-482d-a24c-895e620e635f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:46.747Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"48\n$sources $skip $mats bed bed-floor campfire-bricks crop-pumpkin crops-bamboo-stage-a fence-simple-high fence-simple-low lily-large log-large pot-large pot-small rock-small-g statue-column statue-column-damaged statue-head statue-obelisk stone-small-flat-a stone-small-g stone-small-h stone-tall-b stone-tall-c stone-tall-e stump-round stump-square-detailed tent-detailed-closed tent-small-closed tree-blocks tree-cone tree-default tree-default-dark tree-detailed tree-fat tree-fat-fall tree-oak tree-oak-fall tree-pine-default-a tree-pine-ground-a tree-pine-round-a tree-pine-round-d tree-pine-small-a tree-pine-small-c tree-pine-tall-c tree-pine-tall-d-detailed tree-small tree-tall\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AtPC2RqATx4t2fCmzDzWSL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
