{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TEPEQ77RXFtD7LHC9Qt1Qs","type":"tool_result","content":"### 6.2 Sites\n\n| Site | Vantage | Distances | Bucks | Time | Spawns (outline) | Critters |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 20-60 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |\n| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 40-110 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |\n| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 30-90 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |\n| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 50-90 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |\n| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 120-220 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |\n| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 60-100 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |\n| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 40-90 m | 2 (+3 cows, a calf) | 70 s | moose wade through reeds (legs below the water); a cow and calf cross close | ducks (150), beaver (100), loons (-400) |\n| Muskeg 2 **Spruce Bog** | a bog edge in fog | 25-60 m | 3 | 70 s | fog banks drift; moose loom out close; one stands and stares instead of running | snowshoe hare (125), raven (100) |\n| Muskeg 3 **Burn Clearing** | a snowy rise over the burn | 60-120 m | 3 | 75 s | moose trot across; two bulls lock antlers (fight) then split; a wolf pack chases a cow through (don't hit her) | wolves x3 (300), raven (100) |\n\n### 6.3 Trophies","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"042dbc2a-9d29-45a3-af80-e698e6bece31","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:25:06.293Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 6.2 Sites\n\n| Site | Vantage | Distances | Bucks | Time | Spawns (outline) | Critters |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 20-60 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |\n| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 40-110 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |\n| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 30-90 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |\n| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 50-90 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |\n| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 120-220 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |\n| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 60-100 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |\n| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 40-90 m | 2 (