s | Time | Spawns (outline) | Critters |"," |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 36° | 20-60 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |","-| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 30° | 40-110 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |","-| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 34° | 30-90 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |","-| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 30° | 50-90 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |","-| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 22° | 120-220 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |","-| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 28° | 60-100 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |","-| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 32° | 40-90 m | 2 (+3 cows, a calf) | 70 s | moose wade through reeds (legs below the water); a cow and calf cross close | ducks (150), beaver (100), loons (-400) |","-| Muskeg 2 **Spruce Bog** | a bog edge in fog | 38° | 25-60 m | 3 | 70 s | fog banks drift; moose loom out close; one stands and stares instead of running | snowshoe hare (125), raven (100) |","-| Muskeg 3 **Burn Clearing** | a snowy rise over the burn | 30° | 60-120 m | 3 | 75 s | moose trot across; two bulls lock antlers (fight) then split; a wolf pack chases a cow through (don't hit her) | wolves x3 (300), raven (100) |","-","-FOV is the vertical field of view in degrees (telephoto-ish, so animals read at 480 x 270: a deer at 40 m is","-about 30 px tall at 30°); the scope multiplies it down by its magnification.","+| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 34° | 18-50 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |","+| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 28° | 30-90 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |","+| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 32° | 25-70 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |","+| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 28° | 40-80 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |","+| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 22° | 100-180 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |","+| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 26° | 50-90 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |","+| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 30° | 35-80 m | 2 (+3 cows, a calf) | 70 s | moose wade through reeds (legs below the water); a cow and calf cross close | ducks (150), beaver (100), loons (-400) |","+| Muskeg 2 **Spruce Bog** | a bog edge in fog | 36° | 20-50 m | 3 | 70 s | fog banks drift; moose loom out close; one stands and stares instead of running | snowshoe hare (125), raven (100) |","+| Muskeg 3 **Burn Clearing** | a snowy rise over the burn | 26° | 50-110 m | 3 | 75 s | moose trot across; two bulls lock antlers (fight) then split; a wolf pack chases a cow through (don't hit her) | wolves x3 (300), raven (100) |","+","+FOV is the vertical field of view in degrees, telephoto-ish so animals read at 480 x 270: at 28° a whitetail (head","+up, about 23 units tall before the `animalScale` boost) is about 26 px tall at 30 m, 16 px at 50 m and 10 px at 80 m,","+where the scope (x3.5) makes it 34 px. Keep most shots inside 90 m; longer ones are scope shots by design."," "," ### 6.3 Trophies"," "," | Trophy | Where | Rules |"," |---|---|---|","-| **Old Iron Rack** (14-point whitetail) | Fog Glade at dawn, 70-120 m, 45 s | appears in 3 windows of 3.5 s between fog banks; a doe walks in front of him in window 3; he ignores calls until window 3 (then freezes 1.0 s) |","-| **The Duke of Bugle Ridge** (7 x 7 bull elk) | dark timber edge, 80-140 m, 50 s | he bugles from the trees (panned left or right so you can hear where); each of your calls draws him to the next opening for 4 s (4 openings); a cow leads him through the second; calling a fifth time sends him off |","-| **Big Mo** (72-inch bull moose) | the lake shore, 120 m in to 20 m, 45 s | bursts from the reeds and charges the stand over about 8 s; a lethal hit drops him; a gut or ham hit slows him; at 15 m he flattens the stand (screen tilt and crash: BIG MO SAYS NO!) and the trophy is lost; if missed he retreats and charges again, three times |","+| **Old Iron Rack** (14-point whitetail) | Fog Glade at dawn, 60-100 m, 45 s | appears in 3 windows of 3.5 s between fog banks; a doe walks in front of him in window 3; he ignores calls until window 3 (then freezes 1.0 s) |","+| **The Duke of Bugle Ridge** (7 x 7 bull elk) | dark timber edge, 70-120 m, 50 s | he bugles from the trees (panned left or right so you can hear where); each of your calls draws him to the next opening for 4 s (4 openings); a cow leads him through the second; calling a fifth time sends him off |","+| **Big Mo** (72-inch bull moose) | the lake shore, 110 m in to 20 m, 45 s | bursts from the reeds and charges the stand over about 8 s; a lethal hit drops him; a gut or ham hit slows him; at 15 m he flattens the stand (screen tilt and crash: BIG MO SAYS NO!) and the trophy is lost; if missed he retreats and charges again, three times |"," "," ### 6.4 Bonus games (30 s each)"," "]},{"oldStart":1321,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1322,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | heartMult / headMult / lungMult | 2.0 / 1.8 / 1.6 | 0.5-4 | zone multipliers |"," | runningMult | 1.25 | 1-2 | running-shot multiplier |"," | antlerBoost | 1.15 | 1-2 | antler drawing scale |","+| animalScale | 1.1 | 0.8-1.5 | arcade size boost for every animal (drawing and hit zones together) |"," | fog | 1.0 | 0-2 | fog density (look) |"," | timeOfDay | 0 | -1..1 | shifts the sun and grade (look) |"," | timeScale | 1.0 | 0.1-2 | game speed |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013dSngpaqpG79eHcjAzaQLz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
