{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh223Nm9z7MLyLNRBahr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QfZyKHz7cZkDQEiAYfoEiG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work; python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\nreps = [\n(\"\"\"- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit leg's stride cut) and\n  heads for the nearest exit; any further hit kills it; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST** (a penalty).\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp; at 0 it dies. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit\n  leg's stride cut) and heads for the nearest exit; further hits take more hp; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST**\n  (a penalty).\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (so a moose survives two gut shots). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (a lethal zone kills any of them; a deer drops to two gut shots, a moose to\nfour). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"kill points = round( base(species, antlers) x distanceMult x zoneMult x (running ? 1.25 : 1) x (trophy ? 3 : 1) ) + quick + multi\"\"\",\n \"\"\"kill points = round( base(species, antlers) x distanceMult x zoneMult x (running ? 1.25 : 1) x (trophy ? 3 : 1) ) + quick + multi\nrunning = the animal was moving faster than its species' trot speed when hit; zoneMult = the killing shot's zone\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n  score, stats; benching is per player; the site ends when every non-benched player has nothing left to shoot or time\n  runs out.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n  score, stats; benching is per player (benched players watch); the site's end rules (5.7) apply to everyone.\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Reconcile wound/hp rules and clarify running and party end rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5834,"cache_read_input_tokens":442375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5834},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"531a9471-a7ab-4a13-9e38-e9c6c4a8415b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:17.997Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh22388aXw8RXzcbEy5H","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QfZyKHz7cZkDQEiAYfoEiG":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work; python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\nreps = [\n(\"\"\"- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit leg's stride cut) and\n  heads for the nearest exit; any further hit kills it; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST** (a penalty).\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp; at 0 it dies. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit\n  leg's stride cut) and heads for the nearest exit; further hits take more hp; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST**\n  (a penalty).\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (so a moose survives two gut shots). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (a lethal zone kills any of them; a deer drops to two gut shots, a moose to\nfour). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"kill points = round( base(species, antlers) x distanceMult x zoneMult x (running ? 1.25 : 1) x (trophy ? 3 : 1) ) + quick + multi\"\"\",\n \"\"\"kill points = round( base(species, antlers) x distanceMult x zoneMult x (running ? 1.25 : 1) x (trophy ? 3 : 1) ) + quick + multi\nrunning = the animal was moving faster than its species' trot speed when hit; zoneMult = the killing shot's zone\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n  score, stats; benching is per player; the site ends when every non-benched player has nothing left to shoot or time\n  runs out.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n  score, stats; benching is per player (benched players watch); the site's end rules (5.7) apply to everyone.\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Reconcile wound/hp rules and clarify running and party end rules"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QfZyKHz7cZkDQEiAYfoEiG","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"8bb309f1-6216-43fd-addf-0e73f6ebf091","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:18.414Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1581,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1581,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e\",\"uuid\":\"a7fa48a6-865a-469c-aa39-21762f7cd5f4\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3000,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e\",\"uuid\":\"233a8867-e1c6-4cf7-ad26-76a2313a2a94\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e\",\"uuid\":\"1c39c257-7777-4149-b396-46bc8f136d42\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e\",\"uuid\":\"acade492-cdf7-4acc-a374-3b8f1b97a95f\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1892,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1892,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":40800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"69a10fc6-94fe-45a4-a5f1-6399da753053\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":40900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"62190675-445d-4f8c-80a3-040e2632487f\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":41000,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"df7bd741-74d3-4e7b-b3c6-686cc0f20388\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":41100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"9f5c4841-d327-43e4-9563-78ef86311d9f\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1578,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1578,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6\",\"uuid\":\"fa2530e1-c9b4-4b3d-8abc-c1216f70e74f\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6\",\"uuid\":\"fc7358b4-76b7-4797-a2d9-05a60a5d3ea4\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6\",\"uuid\":\"28fc01b1-3025-467e-96d2-60e55945ca17\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6\",\"uuid\":\"03ef66ad-21c4-4e04-a094-12d6d1500274\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":563,"oldLines":8,"newStart":563,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - **Calls** (5.8): within the call's radius, animals that are not panicking stop and look toward the caller for","   `callFreeze` seconds (1.4 +- 0.2), then go on (moose may take a few steps toward you). Each animal answers a call at","   most twice per site. Bull elk may bugle back. Trophies have their own rules (6.3).","-- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit leg's stride cut) and","-  heads for the nearest exit; any further hit kills it; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST** (a penalty). A killed","+- **Wounds and death**: zone damage (5.9) reduces hp; at 0 it dies. A wounded animal limps (speed x0.6, the hit","+  leg's stride cut) and heads for the nearest exit; further hits take more hp; if it leaves the frame it is **LOST**","+  (a penalty). A killed","   animal plays `dying` then lies `dead` with a tag over it (the bagger's colour, its points) until the site ends."," - **Exits**: an animal past its path's end or outside the camera's bearing range plus 10 degrees is `gone`; a buck","   that goes is **ESCAPED** (its HUD icon is crossed out)."]},{"oldStart":700,"oldLines":7,"newStart":701,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Zones are rebuilt from the joints every step (they bend, run and fall with the rig) and every zone stays inside the"," drawn body, so a shot just off the silhouette misses."," ","-Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (so a moose survives two gut shots). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig.","+Hit points: whitetail 1, elk 1.5, moose 2 (a lethal zone kills any of them; a deer drops to two gut shots, a moose to","+four). Elk and moose zones scale with the rig."," Effects by what was hit: fur puff and thump (animal), feathers (bird), bark chips and a wood knock (trunk), sparks and a"," ricochet whine (rock), dirt clods and a thud (terrain), a splash column (water), nothing but the echo (sky). Every shot"," emits spook noise (5.6). Same-step hits on one animal by two players: the better zone gets it; equal zones share the"]},{"oldStart":719,"oldLines":6,"newStart":721,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ```"," kill points = round( base(species, antlers) x distanceMult x zoneMult x (running ? 1.25 : 1) x (trophy ? 3 : 1) ) + quick + multi","+running = the animal was moving faster than its species' trot speed when hit; zoneMult = the killing shot's zone"," base: whitetail 100 + 15 per point; elk 150 + 20 per point; moose 200 + 6 per inch of spread"," distanceMult = clamp(1 + (metres - 25) / 75, 1, 3.5)          (100 m = 2.0; 175 m = 3.0)"," quick = +50 if the kill comes within 1.0 s of the buck first being visible"]},{"oldStart":749,"oldLines":8,"newStart":752,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Colours are the AI Hub seat colours: P1 `#e8443a` red, P2 `#3b82f6` blue, P3 `#22c55e` green, P4 `#f5b700` gold,","   plus the reticle shapes (5.8) so colour is never the only cue."," - Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,","-  score, stats; benching is per player; the site ends when every non-benched player has nothing left to shoot or time","-  runs out.","+  score, stats; benching is per player (benched players watch); the site's end rules (5.7) apply to everyone."," - The tally shows a column per player; hunt results show a podium; the winner may enter initials."," - A pad unplugged pauses with the engine's message (per player)."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QfZyKHz7cZkDQEiAYfoEiG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh23QzK9kqztF9x17LGT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G2JYuTXrYrEHrjQMSts5Ax","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","offset":770,"limit":140},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":448209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1930},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"87d03681-2164-4fbd-b7dc-ec36b3302315","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:21.723Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh23QiC26duKyhd9dD8B","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01G2JYuTXrYrEHrjQMSts5Ax":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","offset":770,"limit":140}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2JYuTXrYrEHrjQMSts5Ax","type":"tool_result","content":"770\t- **Player panels** (P1 bottom left, P2 bottom right, P3 top left, P4 top right): score, five shell icons with a\n771\t  chamber light, call charges (horn icons), breath arc while scoped, BENCHED tag.\n772\t- **Centre banners**: BUCKS ONLY!, HEART SHOT!, DOE! YOU'RE OUT!, TROPHY!, TIME!, with an extruded `E.font.title`\n773\t  style, 0.9 s, a whoosh.\n774\t- **Score pops** in the world over the animal: \"+425 HEART SHOT 86 m\" in the shooter's colour.\n775\t- **Captions** (barks and dialog) lower centre with the speaker's name and colour.\n776\t- **Prompts** lower centre, contextual (PUMP!, HOLD [L2] TO SCOPE, CALL [△]), shown only when relevant and for a\n777\t  limited number of times per hunt.\n778\t- **Rival tag** (campaign): top left under P3's place: \"DWAYNE 4,600\".\n779\t- **Hold to see standings** (Tab or Create; unbound in hub rounds): a centre table of players' scores.\n780\t\n781\t**Glyphs**: `Prompts.label(action, player)` decides the family by the player's last device: `gamepad` -> the pad's\n782\tglyph (`input.label(action, 'gamepad')` gives '✕', '○', '□', '△', 'R2', 'L2', 'R1', 'L1' with PlayStation symbols, or\n783\t'A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'RT', 'LT', 'RB', 'LB' with Xbox); `keyboard` or `mouse` -> one KB+M family: actions bound to a\n784\tmouse button show the mouse icon once the mouse has been used this session, others show the key (R, Q, Shift, Space,\n785\tEsc, Tab, Enter). `52-glyphs.js` draws each as a pixel icon: PS shapes in their colours (blue cross, red circle, pink\n786\tsquare, green triangle) on dark discs, trigger and bumper tabs, stick icons, Options and Create pills; Xbox letters on\n787\tcoloured discs; keycaps (wide for Space, Shift, Enter); a mouse with the left, right or wheel highlighted. The default\n788\tbutton symbols are **PlayStation**; Settings > Controller > Button symbols offers Xbox (engine setting, default changed:\n789\tAppendix C).\n790\t\n791\t**Tests** (unit/prompts): with a pad last used, labels are PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox letters after\n792\t`settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`; with the mouse used, fire shows the left-click icon and pump shows R; every action\n793\tthe HUD prompts has an icon in all three families; every caption and banner fits the screen width at its scale\n794\t(`E.font.width`).\n795\t\n796\t### 5.13 Feedback and juice\n797\t- Shot: a 1-2 px screen shake (comfort setting respected), reticle bloom, gunshot with a valley echo (5.20), a pad\n798\t  rumble (0.35, 0.08 s) for the shooter.\n799\t- Kill: hit-stop 0.04 s (`game.freeze`), callout banner for lethal zones, score pop, the bagged tag; a stronger rumble.\n800\t- Doe: a red-tinted flash (flashes setting respected), the sad-trombone sting, the emcee's groan, the BENCHED reticle.\n801\t- Multi-kills, long shots (150 m and more: LONG SHOT!), running shots: their own barks.\n802\t- **Trophy Cam** (trophy kills, and in single player the last buck of a site if it was a heart shot; setting On /\n803\t  Trophies only / Off): the sim runs at `game.timeScale = 0.15` while the camera flight takes 1.4 s of unscaled time\n804\t  (`game.real`): the lens flies from the vantage along the shot's ray to 3 m from the impact, the fov narrows, a\n805\t  bullet streak leads; at impact the animal flashes to its x-ray look (skeleton, heart and lungs) for 0.35 s; normal\n806\t  speed for its collapse; back to the vantage with a fade; time scale restored. Skippable (confirm). Never during local multiplayer or hub rounds (they show the Shot Chart\n807\t  only). Under Reduce motion it is a still x-ray card.\n808\t- Skunk: a green dithered cloud over 60% of the screen fading over 3 s, a \"pfft\" and a stink chord.\n809\t\n810\t### 5.14 Tally and the Shot Chart (`60-tally.js`)\n811\tA full-screen card over the dimmed, frozen vista, one beat at a time (10-foot friendly), confirm to skip ahead:\n812\t1. SITE CLEAR or TIME!, the site's name.\n813\t2. For each bagged animal, a card: its x-ray side view (`rig.drawXray`: a dithered translucent body, skeleton lines,\n814\t   heart red and lungs pink, entry marks where each round went, labelled HEART / LUNG / GUT...), its distance, antler\n815\t   points or spread, and its points line counted up with ticks.\n816\t3. Critters, penalties, accuracy, clean sweep, no-penalty bonus, site total; the stars (antler icons) pop in.\n817\t4. Party: a column per player, then the site's leader. Campaign: the standings strip against the rivals.\n818\tPrompt: [✕] CONTINUE (per device). Confirm is ignored for the first 0.6 s (Space pumps in play and confirms here, so\n819\ta late pump doesn't skip a card). Auto-advances after 12 s in the attract mode.\n820\t\n821\t### 5.15 Trophy encounters (`61-trophy.js`)\n822\tA trophy site is a site with a legend, one named animal and rules of its own (6.3). Shared parts: a campfire legend\n823\tdialog before it (Uncle Dub), tension music layers in when the trophy is on screen, the trophy shows a TROPHY tag the\n824\tfirst time it's seen, its HUD icon is gold, it has 1.5x the species' hp and ignores the call except where its rules\n825\tsay, and a miss makes it bolt (its window ends). Bagged: Trophy Cam, TROPHY BAGGED!, x3 points, its mount unlocks in\n826\tthe Lodge. Escaped: THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY (no penalty). Saved in records either way (seen, bagged, best distance).\n827\t\n828\t### 5.16 Bonus games (`62-bonus.js`)\n829\tA framework for 30-second shooting galleries on the same landscape at a bonus vantage: a target spawner on a\n830\ttimeline, thrown or flying targets on ballistic arcs (`E.arc`-style maths in world space) or `E.Path`s, the same rifle\n831\trules with a bigger tube and faster rack, per-target points, protected targets with penalties, a PERFECT bonus (every\n832\ttarget hit with no misses doubles the bonus total), and a bonus tally. The three games are in 6.4. Bonus Only mode plays\n833\tany of them from the menu; they keep their own high-score tables.\n834\t\n835\t### 5.17 Modes and menus (`90-91-92-94`, `53-ui.js`)\n836\t\n837\t**Title**: the logo (`E.font.title`, wood-and-brass gradient with a blaze-orange outline, \"THE 41ST ANNUAL\" above it)\n838\tover a live vista (Hollow Creek at dawn, deer grazing, slow pan); PRESS [START] in the last device's glyph; the\n839\tengine's corner menu button (settings) at top right. CONTINUE appears in the menu when an autosaved Hunt-Off exists.\n840\t\n841\t**Main menu** (big cards, one column, focus with d-pad, stick or arrows; hover with the mouse moves the focus; click or\n842\tconfirm picks; cancel goes back; a prompt bar at the bottom shows confirm and back glyphs):\n843\t\n844\t| Entry | What it does |\n845\t|---|---|\n846\t| HUNT-OFF (or CONTINUE HUNT-OFF) | the campaign: Hollow Creek, Bugle Ridge, Muskeg Lake in order, rivals and standings, ceremony; autosave after each hunt (`game.saves` autosave slot) |\n847\t| SINGLE HUNT | pick one of the three hunts (card with species, time of day, trophy silhouette, best score) |\n848\t| PARTY HUNT | the join page (players press Options or Start on their pads; the mouse player is P1), then pick a hunt or QUICK DRAW (site 1 of each hunt plus Saucer Season, time-boxed; a short loading card raises each landscape between them) |\n849\t| BONUS GAMES | pick Crow Patrol, Saucer Season or Snowball Standoff |\n850\t| PRACTICE RANGE | Uncle Dub's range: the tutorial (6.5) |\n851\t| THE LODGE | the trophy room (5.18) |\n852\t| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen (`game.menu('settings')`) |\n853\t| ABOUT & CREDITS | 5.27 |\n854\t\n855\t**Difficulty** (picked on the hunt card, remembered): Easy (Strong assist, auto-pump, animals x0.85 speed, +1 call),\n856\tNormal, Pro (no assist, animals x1.15 speed, does mixed in more often, scope sway x1.3).\n857\t\n858\t### 5.18 The Lodge, records and saves (`93-lodge.js`)\n859\t- A cozy side-view room built with the engine's own 2D pipeline: a `side` view, a PlatformMap floor of `wood` tiles and\n860\t  a log back wall (`back` tiles, `plank` material), engine props and shapes (fireplace from custom shape, table, chairs,\n861\t  bench, bookcase, barrel, lamps; `light: true`), warm canvas lighting with a flickering fire, Uncle Dub in a rocking\n862\t  chair (Humanoid, idle; waves when focused), a sleeping hound (Blob).\n863\t- The trophy wall: plaques for Old Iron Rack, The Duke, Big Mo (dark silhouettes until bagged, then `rig.drawMount`),\n864\t  each hunt's best buck, and the records chalkboard (E.Arcade tables per mode with initials, preloaded with DUB, MAE,\n865\t  DWN, LOR, ERL). Focus moves along the wall (d-pad, stick, arrows, mouse hover); the camera pans to it; a big info\n866\t  card shows its story, distance, date bagged.\n867\t- Stats card: hunts played, shots, accuracy, bucks bagged, does shot, longest shot, favourite rifle sound (a joke line).\n868\t- `Records` in `E.store`: best scores per mode and hunt, stars per site, trophies, stats, the Range badge. In AI Hub\n869\t  sessions storage is a throwaway memory store (the client's), so nothing special is needed.\n870\t\n871\t### 5.19 Dialog, barks and voices (`71-barks.js`, `babble.js`)\n872\t- **Dialog** scenes use `E.Dialog` with Humanoid portraits; `voice: null` and our Babble voice plays the line. Story\n873\t  beats are data (`def('beat', ...)`): a list of `[speaker, line]` with optional pose and expression.\n874\t- **Barks**: categories (6.9) with 3-6 lines each; picked without repeating the last two (fx stream); the emcee shouts\n875\t  them as a caption plus a short Babble burst; at most one bark per 1.2 s, high-priority barks (doe, trophy, triple)\n876\t  cut in.\n877\t- **E.Babble** (Animalese/Simlish style): each line becomes syllables (letter pairs; vowels pick the pitch step),\n878\t  12-16 syllables a second, each a 40-70 ms blip through a band-pass \"formant\" filter per vowel; per character: base\n879\t  pitch, waveform, speed, pitch spread, warble. Exclamations rise at the end; questions rise; ALL-CAPS barks are louder\n880\t  and faster. Voices: Emcee (140 Hz square, boomy, echo), Uncle Dub (105 Hz saw with noise grit, slow), Granny Mae (260\n881\t  Hz sine with vibrato), Dwayne (185 Hz 12.5% pulse, nasal), Loretta (225 Hz triangle, bright), Earl (95 Hz square,\n882\t  slow and warm). Uses `game.audio.ctx` and the exposed sfx bus (Appendix C); silent headless.\n883\t\n884\t### 5.20 Audio (`70-audio.js`)\n885\t\n886\t**Music** (engine song notation; bluegrass chiptune):\n887\t\n888\t| Song | Where | Sketch |\n889\t|---|---|---|\n890\t| `hoedown` | title, menus | 140 bpm, G major: pulse-25% banjo rolls in 16ths, square fiddle melody, triangle root-fifth bass, washboard noise and rimshots |\n891\t| `lodgefire` | Lodge, About | 84 bpm, warm square \"harmonica\" with vibrato over triangle chords, soft brushes |\n892\t| `stalk` | hunt sites (layers) | 96 bpm pads and pulse ostinato at low volume; layer `drums` comes in when bucks are on screen, layer `tension` (heartbeat kick, tremolo) when a trophy is on screen (`audio.layer`) |\n893\t| `jamboree` | bonus games | 160 bpm hoedown, fast fiddle |\n894\t| `results` | tallies, hunt results | 110 bpm strut |\n895\t| `fanfare`, `siteclear`, `doe`, `escaped`, `newrecord` | stings (`audio.sting`) | trophy fanfare; clear jingle; sad trombone slide; two-note fall; initials theme |\n896\t\n897\t**Ambience** beds per hunt: wind (filtered noise, slow swells), birdsong chirps (random sine and pulse blips by time of\n898\tday), creek or lake lapping, distant crows (Hollow), elk chirps and distant bugles (Bugle), loon calls and ice creaks\n899\t(Muskeg).\n900\t\n901\t**SFX** (engine voices, lists with `delay` for layering): rifle shot (noise crack 0.05 s high-passed + 60 Hz sine\n902\tthump 0.15 s + low noise tail 0.6 s + two echoes at 0.35 s and 0.8 s, quieter and darker, the echo delay longer across\n903\topen valleys); dry click; pump rack (two band-passed clicks 0.09 s apart with a slide); shell inserts; scope raise\n904\t(cloth swish); breath in and out; calls (grunt: 90 Hz saw wobble; bugle: sine 500 -> 1800 Hz glide with vibrato and\n905\ta noisy scream; moose: 70 Hz saw \"waugh\"); impacts (fur thump, wood knock, rock ricochet whine 3000 -> 1200 Hz,\n906\tdirt thud, splash); hooves by gait; animal voices (snort, cow-elk chirp, turkey gobble trill, duck quack, crow caw,\n907\tsquirrel chatter, marmot whistle, wolf and coyote howls, loon wail, beaver slap); crow flap; clay break; scarecrow\n908\tbonk; snowball splat; UI focus tick, confirm, back; score ticks; banner whoosh; stink; slow-mo whoosh.\n909\tA Sound Lab dev scene plays every song, sfx and voice for review."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"e3ced682-6435-4519-90e9-7e44cb6a4460","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:21.729Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Player panels** (P1 bottom left, P2 bottom right, P3 top left, P4 top right): score, five shell icons with a\n  chamber light, call charges (horn icons), breath arc while scoped, BENCHED tag.\n- **Centre banners**: BUCKS ONLY!, HEART SHOT!, DOE! YOU'RE OUT!, TROPHY!, TIME!, with an extruded `E.font.title`\n  style, 0.9 s, a whoosh.\n- **Score pops** in the world over the animal: \"+425 HEART SHOT 86 m\" in the shooter's colour.\n- **Captions** (barks and dialog) lower centre with the speaker's name and colour.\n- **Prompts** lower centre, contextual (PUMP!, HOLD [L2] TO SCOPE, CALL [△]), shown only when relevant and for a\n  limited number of times per hunt.\n- **Rival tag** (campaign): top left under P3's place: \"DWAYNE 4,600\".\n- **Hold to see standings** (Tab or Create; unbound in hub rounds): a centre table of players' scores.\n\n**Glyphs**: `Prompts.label(action, player)` decides the family by the player's last device: `gamepad` -> the pad's\nglyph (`input.label(action, 'gamepad')` gives '✕', '○', '□', '△', 'R2', 'L2', 'R1', 'L1' with PlayStation symbols, or\n'A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'RT', 'LT', 'RB', 'LB' with Xbox); `keyboard` or `mouse` -> one KB+M family: actions bound to a\nmouse button show the mouse icon once the mouse has been used this session, others show the key (R, Q, Shift, Space,\nEsc, Tab, Enter). `52-glyphs.js` draws each as a pixel icon: PS shapes in their colours (blue cross, red circle, pink\nsquare, green triangle) on dark discs, trigger and bumper tabs, stick icons, Options and Create pills; Xbox letters on\ncoloured discs; keycaps (wide for Space, Shift, Enter); a mouse with the left, right or wheel highlighted. The default\nbutton symbols are **PlayStation**; Settings > Controller > Button symbols offers Xbox (engine setting, default changed:\nAppendix C).\n\n**Tests** (unit/prompts): with a pad last used, labels are PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox letters after\n`settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`; with the mouse used, fire shows the left-click icon and pump shows R; every action\nthe HUD prompts has an icon in all three families; every caption and banner fits the screen width at its scale\n(`E.font.width`).\n\n### 5.13 Feedback and juice\n- Shot: a 1-2 px screen shake (comfort setting respected), reticle bloom, gunshot with a valley echo (5.20), a pad\n  rumble (0.35, 0.08 s) for the shooter.\n- Kill: hit-stop 0.04 s (`game.freeze`), callout banner for lethal zones, score pop, the bagged tag; a stronger rumble.\n- Doe: a red-tinted flash (flashes setting respected), the sad-trombone sting, the emcee's groan, the BENCHED reticle.\n- Multi-kills, long shots (150 m and more: LONG SHOT!), running shots: their own barks.\n- **Trophy Cam** (trophy kills, and in single player the last buck of a site if it was a heart shot; setting On /\n  Trophies only / Off): the sim runs at `game.timeScale = 0.15` while the camera flight takes 1.4 s of unscaled time\n  (`game.real`): the lens flies from the vantage along the shot's ray to 3 m from the impact, the fov narrows, a\n  bullet streak leads; at impact the animal flashes to its x-ray look (skeleton, heart and lungs) for 0.35 s; normal\n  speed for its collapse; back to the vantage with a fade; time scale restored. Skippable (confirm). Never during local multiplayer or hub rounds (they show the Shot Chart\n  only). Under Reduce motion it is a still x-ray card.\n- Skunk: a green dithered cloud over 60% of the screen fading over 3 s, a \"pfft\" and a stink chord.\n\n### 5.14 Tally and the Shot Chart (`60-tally.js`)\nA full-screen card over the dimmed, frozen vista, one beat at a time (10-foot friendly), confirm to skip ahead:\n1. SITE CLEAR or TIME!, the site's name.\n2. For each bagged animal, a card: its x-ray side view (`rig.drawXray`: a dithered translucent body, skeleton lines,\n   heart red and lungs pink, entry marks where each round went, labelled HEART / LUNG / GUT...), its distance, antler\n   points or spread, and its points line counted up with ticks.\n3. Critters, penalties, accuracy, clean sweep, no-penalty bonus, site total; the stars (antler icons) pop in.\n4. Party: a column per player, then the site's leader. Campaign: the standings strip against the rivals.\nPrompt: [✕] CONTINUE (per device). Confirm is ignored for the first 0.6 s (Space pumps in play and confirms here, so\na late pump doesn't skip a card). Auto-advances after 12 s in the attract mode.\n\n### 5.15 Trophy encounters (`61-trophy.js`)\nA trophy site is a site with a legend, one named animal and rules of its own (6.3). Shared parts: a campfire legend\ndialog before it (Uncle Dub), tension music layers in when the trophy is on screen, the trophy shows a TROPHY tag the\nfirst time it's seen, its HUD icon is gold, it has 1.5x the species' hp and ignores the call except where its rules\nsay, and a miss makes it bolt (its window ends). Bagged: Trophy Cam, TROPHY BAGGED!, x3 points, its mount unlocks in\nthe Lodge. Escaped: THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY (no penalty). Saved in records either way (seen, bagged, best distance).\n\n### 5.16 Bonus games (`62-bonus.js`)\nA framework for 30-second shooting galleries on the same landscape at a bonus vantage: a target spawner on a\ntimeline, thrown or flying targets on ballistic arcs (`E.arc`-style maths in world space) or `E.Path`s, the same rifle\nrules with a bigger tube and faster rack, per-target points, protected targets with penalties, a PERFECT bonus (every\ntarget hit with no misses doubles the bonus total), and a bonus tally. The three games are in 6.4. Bonus Only mode plays\nany of them from the menu; they keep their own high-score tables.\n\n### 5.17 Modes and menus (`90-91-92-94`, `53-ui.js`)\n\n**Title**: the logo (`E.font.title`, wood-and-brass gradient with a blaze-orange outline, \"THE 41ST ANNUAL\" above it)\nover a live vista (Hollow Creek at dawn, deer grazing, slow pan); PRESS [START] in the last device's glyph; the\nengine's corner menu button (settings) at top right. CONTINUE appears in the menu when an autosaved Hunt-Off exists.\n\n**Main menu** (big cards, one column, focus with d-pad, stick or arrows; hover with the mouse moves the focus; click or\nconfirm picks; cancel goes back; a prompt bar at the bottom shows confirm and back glyphs):\n\n| Entry | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| HUNT-OFF (or CONTINUE HUNT-OFF) | the campaign: Hollow Creek, Bugle Ridge, Muskeg Lake in order, rivals and standings, ceremony; autosave after each hunt (`game.saves` autosave slot) |\n| SINGLE HUNT | pick one of the three hunts (card with species, time of day, trophy silhouette, best score) |\n| PARTY HUNT | the join page (players press Options or Start on their pads; the mouse player is P1), then pick a hunt or QUICK DRAW (site 1 of each hunt plus Saucer Season, time-boxed; a short loading card raises each landscape between them) |\n| BONUS GAMES | pick Crow Patrol, Saucer Season or Snowball Standoff |\n| PRACTICE RANGE | Uncle Dub's range: the tutorial (6.5) |\n| THE LODGE | the trophy room (5.18) |\n| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen (`game.menu('settings')`) |\n| ABOUT & CREDITS | 5.27 |\n\n**Difficulty** (picked on the hunt card, remembered): Easy (Strong assist, auto-pump, animals x0.85 speed, +1 call),\nNormal, Pro (no assist, animals x1.15 speed, does mixed in more often, scope sway x1.3).\n\n### 5.18 The Lodge, records and saves (`93-lodge.js`)\n- A cozy side-view room built with the engine's own 2D pipeline: a `side` view, a PlatformMap floor of `wood` tiles and\n  a log back wall (`back` tiles, `plank` material), engine props and shapes (fireplace from custom shape, table, chairs,\n  bench, bookcase, barrel, lamps; `light: true`), warm canvas lighting with a flickering fire, Uncle Dub in a rocking\n  chair (Humanoid, idle; waves when focused), a sleeping hound (Blob).\n- The trophy wall: plaques for Old Iron Rack, The Duke, Big Mo (dark silhouettes until bagged, then `rig.drawMount`),\n  each hunt's best buck, and the records chalkboard (E.Arcade tables per mode with initials, preloaded with DUB, MAE,\n  DWN, LOR, ERL). Focus moves along the wall (d-pad, stick, arrows, mouse hover); the camera pans to it; a big info\n  card shows its story, distance, date bagged.\n- Stats card: hunts played, shots, accuracy, bucks bagged, does shot, longest shot, favourite rifle sound (a joke line).\n- `Records` in `E.store`: best scores per mode and hunt, stars per site, trophies, stats, the Range badge. In AI Hub\n  sessions storage is a throwaway memory store (the client's), so nothing special is needed.\n\n### 5.19 Dialog, barks and voices (`71-barks.js`, `babble.js`)\n- **Dialog** scenes use `E.Dialog` with Humanoid portraits; `voice: null` and our Babble voice plays the line. Story\n  beats are data (`def('beat', ...)`): a list of `[speaker, line]` with optional pose and expression.\n- **Barks**: categories (6.9) with 3-6 lines each; picked without repeating the last two (fx stream); the emcee shouts\n  them as a caption plus a short Babble burst; at most one bark per 1.2 s, high-priority barks (doe, trophy, triple)\n  cut in.\n- **E.Babble** (Animalese/Simlish style): each line becomes syllables (letter pairs; vowels pick the pitch step),\n  12-16 syllables a second, each a 40-70 ms blip through a band-pass \"formant\" filter per vowel; per character: base\n  pitch, waveform, speed, pitch spread, warble. Exclamations rise at the end; questions rise; ALL-CAPS barks are louder\n  and faster. Voices: Emcee (140 Hz square, boomy, echo), Uncle Dub (105 Hz saw with noise grit, slow), Granny Mae (260\n  Hz sine with vibrato), Dwayne (185 Hz 12.5% pulse, nasal), Loretta (225 Hz triangle, bright), Earl (95 Hz square,\n  slow and warm). Uses `game.audio.ctx` and the exposed sfx bus (Appendix C); silent headless.\n\n### 5.20 Audio (`70-audio.js`)\n\n**Music** (engine song notation; bluegrass chiptune):\n\n| Song | Where | Sketch |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hoedown` | title, menus | 140 bpm, G major: pulse-25% banjo rolls in 16ths, square fiddle melody, triangle root-fifth bass, washboard noise and rimshots |\n| `lodgefire` | Lodge, About | 84 bpm, warm square \"harmonica\" with vibrato over triangle chords, soft brushes |\n| `stalk` | hunt sites (layers) | 96 bpm pads and pulse ostinato at low volume; layer `drums` comes in when bucks are on screen, layer `tension` (heartbeat kick, tremolo) when a trophy is on screen (`audio.layer`) |\n| `jamboree` | bonus games | 160 bpm hoedown, fast fiddle |\n| `results` | tallies, hunt results | 110 bpm strut |\n| `fanfare`, `siteclear`, `doe`, `escaped`, `newrecord` | stings (`audio.sting`) | trophy fanfare; clear jingle; sad trombone slide; two-note fall; initials theme |\n\n**Ambience** beds per hunt: wind (filtered noise, slow swells), birdsong chirps (random sine and pulse blips by time of\nday), creek or lake lapping, distant crows (Hollow), elk chirps and distant bugles (Bugle), loon calls and ice creaks\n(Muskeg).\n\n**SFX** (engine voices, lists with `delay` for layering): rifle shot (noise crack 0.05 s high-passed + 60 Hz sine\nthump 0.15 s + low noise tail 0.6 s + two echoes at 0.35 s and 0.8 s, quieter and darker, the echo delay longer across\nopen valleys); dry click; pump rack (two band-passed clicks 0.09 s apart with a slide); shell inserts; scope raise\n(cloth swish); breath in and out; calls (grunt: 90 Hz saw wobble; bugle: sine 500 -> 1800 Hz glide with vibrato and\na noisy scream; moose: 70 Hz saw \"waugh\"); impacts (fur thump, wood knock, rock ricochet whine 3000 -> 1200 Hz,\ndirt thud, splash); hooves by gait; animal voices (snort, cow-elk chirp, turkey gobble trill, duck quack, crow caw,\nsquirrel chatter, marmot whistle, wolf and coyote howls, loon wail, beaver slap); crow flap; clay break; scarecrow\nbonk; snowball splat; UI focus tick, confirm, back; score ticks; banner whoosh; stink; slow-mo whoosh.\nA Sound Lab dev scene plays every song, sfx and voice for review.","numLines":140,"startLine":770,"totalLines":1422}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G2JYuTXrYrEHrjQMSts5Ax","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
