{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyYrzQB4enLmGrsscsGpXM","type":"tool_result","content":"1192\t## 7. Build order and milestones\n1193\t\n1194\tBuild the spine first, one hunt to a full vertical slice, then widen. Each milestone ends with its tests passing\n1195\t(`node tests/run.mjs`) and, where it says so, screenshots looked at.\n1196\t\n1197\t| # | Milestone | Delivers | Done when |\n1198\t|---|---|---|---|\n1199\t| M0 | Setup | dev folder, engine and hub copies, manifest, build script, dev page, test runner and headless loader, `game.debug` stub with snapshot | `node tests/run.mjs` runs (one smoke test); the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors |\n1200\t| M1 | Gallery on a flat floor | E.Lens, Vista with flat terrain, Backdrop sky, billboards with impostors (library trees and rocks), static deer silhouettes, P1 reticle (mouse and pad), fire with analytic sphere hits, a minimal HUD | shooting a silhouette works by mouse and pad; lens tests pass; screenshot looks like a pixel landscape |\n1201\t| M2 | The deer | E.Quadruped whitetail (skeleton, 4 gaits, poses, antlers, outline, LOD, zones, x-ray, mount), Animal Lab | quadruped tests pass; filmstrips of every gait and the death look right |\n1202\t| M3 | The land | E.Heightfield (base, features, water, ground types, light bake, scatter, occluders), terrain raster with occlusion, water, fog and mist, Hollow Creek map, custom props (corn, reeds, tall grass, birch, barn, stand, blind) | terrain and occlusion tests pass; Hollow's three vantages screenshot well; animals hide behind crests |\n1203\t| M4 | Shooting for real | rifle (pump, tube, reload), scope lens with sway and breath, call, aim assist, full shot resolution with zones, occluders, terrain and water, impacts and particles, scoring v1, banners and pops | weapon, aim, shot and score tests pass; pick-agreement check at 95% |\n1204\t| M5 | Living animals and sites | actors, orders, paths on terrain, herds, spooking, calls, wounds, death, patterns, the site runtime and director, Hollow sites 1-3, the tally and Shot Chart, walk-ins | ai and site flow tests pass; a person can play Hollow Creek's three sites start to finish |\n1205\t| M6 | Vertical slice | Old Iron Rack and the Trophy Cam, the bonus framework and Crow Patrol, hunt results with E.Arcade initials and ranks, records, the Lodge v1, story beats with portraits | the Hollow hunt plays from its card to its results; the slice playthrough test passes |\n1206\t| M7 | Sound and voice | songs, layers and stings, ambience beds, every sfx, gunshot echoes, E.Babble voices, barks and captions, the Sound Lab | every sound plays in the Sound Lab; barks fit on screen; headless runs stay silent |\n1207\t| M8 | Front end | title with logo and live vista, main menu and pages (UIKit), the Shell theme and help, settings, glyph prompts (PS default, Xbox option, KB+M), difficulty, the touch-only gate, the Practice Range | prompts, touch and menu flow tests pass; menus work with pad, keys and mouse hover |\n1208\t| M9 | Party | up to 4 local players: joining, colours and shapes, per-player rifles and HUD panels, benching, shared kills, the director-only camera, party tallies and podium, Quick Draw | party flow tests pass; two pads and a mouse play a hunt together |\n1209\t| M10 | Bugle Ridge and Muskeg Lake | elk and moose presets, canid and cow, the two maps, six sites, The Duke and Big Mo, Saucer Season and Snowball Standoff, all critters, the Hunt-Off campaign with rivals, autosave and ceremony | site tests pass for all 9 sites; the campaign playthrough test passes |\n1210\t| M11 | Attract and dev mode | the idle timer, the attract playlist and HunterBot, dev mode (Shell rows, sliders, reset, tools, overlays, free camera), deep links | attract and dev tests pass |\n1211\t| M12 | AI Hub | session flow, own card, the Hub Hunt-Off timeline, ghosts, reporting, end handling; the bundle with the session client first | hub stub tests pass; the harness passes with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5, and with `scenario=host-leave` |\n1212\t| M13 | Polish and balance | bot balance runs and tuning (pars, rivals, speeds, windows), look passes on every vantage (palettes, fog, props, lights), animation passes, About & Credits with the reports, `exit-interview.json`, final full test run | Definition of done (section 10) holds |\n1213\t\n1214\tKeep the game playable from M1 on; keep the full test command green after every milestone.\n1215\t\n1216\t---\n1217\t\n1218\t## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1219\t\n1220\t| Risk | Why it matters | De-risk |\n1221\t|---|---|---|\n1222\t| **The custom renderer** (column terrain, occlusion of billboards, scope second pass) is slow or wrong | everything is seen through it | M1 ships it with a flat floor behind the final interfaces; M3 adds heights with unit tests for breakpoints and `occY` against brute force; screenshots per vantage. Fallback if hills fail: keep the flat floor and fake relief with Backdrop hill layers and big \"ridge\" billboards; the game logic doesn't change. Performance is out of scope, but keep it playable: typed arrays, no allocation per pixel, impostors, skip billboards fully hidden |\n1223\t| **Animals don't read** (deer at a distance look like blobs; bucks vs does unclear) | the core skill is telling bucks from does | the Animal Lab and filmstrips in M2; strong silhouettes, outlines, antlers always drawn with the readability boost, LOD that never drops antlers; screenshots at 20, 60, 120 and 200 m; the Antler glint assist |\n1224\t| **Hits don't match what you see** | unfair misses kill a shooting game | zones are built from the same joints that are drawn; dev overlay shows volumes and rays; the pick-agreement browser check (95%) every run |\n1225\t| **Gaits slide or pop** | broken animation ruins the look | hoof locking, a planted-hoof test, filmstrips per gait; tune speeds to strides |\n1226\t| **Hub ghost sync** (copies drift apart, spawns differ, protocol misses) | the hub drops games that fail its check | timeline keyed to `AIHub.time()`; cameras scripted; spawn RNG separate from cosmetics; a headless hub stub test; the real harness in M12 with latency and loss; build-time check of the client and metas |\n1227\t| **Input breadth** (mouse absolute vs stick velocity, up to 4 players, prompts by device, glyph defaults, menus by hover) | 10-foot and KB+M must both feel native | one InputRouter per player tested headless with `input.press`, `input.feed` and pad codes; the Range teaches every control with live glyphs |\n1228\t| **Audio that sounds cheap** | gunshots and calls sell the fantasy | layered voices with echoes; the Sound Lab for quick iteration; volume balance pass in M13 |\n1229\t| **Content volume** (9 sites, 3 trophies, 3 bonus games, range) | time | data-driven sites and patterns, one hunt fully done before the others, the dev free camera's bearing/distance readout for authoring, the bot for quick runs |\n1230\t| **Engine assumptions** (overlay drawing bypasses engine lighting, particles, weather, camera; HTML shell over the canvas) | surprises late | own fx, weather and grade from M1; check that the pause menu, settings and corner draw over our overlay in M1 |\n1231\t| **Bundle mistakes** (client not first or edited, missing metas, network calls) | hub rejection, broken file | build-time assertions (3.5); tests run against the bundle as well as the dev page |\n1232\t| **Touch-only false positives** (touch laptops) | blocks real players | needs coarse pointer and no fine pointer; cleared by any key, mouse or pad input |\n1233\t\n1234\t---\n1235\t\n1236\t## 9. Testing\n1237\t\n1238\t### 9.1 One command\n1239\t`node tests/run.mjs` runs every headless suite (unit and flow) in Node with the engine headless (`new E.Game()` has no\n1240\tDOM there; `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact 1/120 s steps; `input.tap`, `hold`, `press`, `feed` drive it;\n1241\t`game.debug.snapshot()` reads it). It prints **only failures** and one line: `214 passed, 0 failed (41.2 s)`; exit code 1\n1242\ton any failure. `node tests/run.mjs <filter>` runs matching suites only: rerun a suite only after changing the code it\n1243\tcovers. Flags: `--browser` adds the Playwright checks (9.3), `--hub` the harness (9.4), `--balance` the bot statistics\n1244\t(9.5, prints a table; not pass/fail). Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit; the tests and\n1245\tyour own looks at screenshots decide.\n1246\t\n1247\tThe loader (`tests/lib/load.mjs`) builds a `vm` context with stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location` with\n1248\ta hash, `matchMedia`, `navigator`, optional `AIHub` stub), loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, the new modules, the asset set\n1249\tand `src/*.js` in manifest order, and returns `{ E, game, D: game.debug, step, tap, hold, press, feed, until }`. A\n1250\tsecond loader extracts the scripts from the built HTML so the bundle itself is smoke-tested.\n1251\t\n1252\t### 9.2 Suites (headless)\n1253\t- **unit/lens, unit/terrain, unit/vista, unit/quadruped, unit/ai, unit/weapon, unit/aim, unit/shot, unit/score,\n1254\t  unit/prompts**: as listed in each system above.\n1255\t- **unit/lint**: no `Math.random` in gameplay files; no TODO-like markers or placeholder text; every registered site,\n1256\t  trophy, bonus, critter, beat and bark id referenced exists; every bark and caption fits the screen at its scale.\n1257\t- **flow/sites**: every site at seeds 1-3 with the cheat bot (clean sweep, early end) and with no shots (time out,\n1258\t  escapes); doe benching; protected critter penalties.\n1259\t- **flow/playthrough** (the scripted playthrough of the whole game): title -> PRESS START -> menu -> HUNT-OFF ->\n1260\t  for each hunt: intro dialog skipped -> 3 sites with the average bot -> tallies -> trophy (cheat bot bags it; Trophy\n1261\t  Cam runs and time scale returns to 1) -> bonus -> results with initials entered -> next hunt (autosave written) ->\n1262\t  ceremony -> Lodge shows 3 trophy mounts -> About pages -> title. Checks at each step through the snapshot; no errors\n1263\t  (`game.errors` empty); total under 30 simulated minutes.\n1264\t- **flow/modes**: Single Hunt for each hunt; Bonus Only for each game; Practice Range with scripted inputs completing\n1265\t  every station; Party with 2 and 4 bots; Quick Draw.\n1266\t- **flow/attract**: 10 s idle on the title starts the attract mode; it cycles through its playlist (snapshot shows each\n1267\t  clip); a key, a mouse move, a pad button each return to the title.\n1268\t- **flow/dev**: 5.22's checks.\n1269\t- **flow/touch**: 5.25's checks.\n1270\t- **flow/hub**: 5.26's checks with the stub.\n1271\t- **flow/determinism**: the same seed and scripted inputs twice give the same `stateHash` after 60 s of a site; a run\n1272\t  with extra cosmetic RNG draws gives the same spawn log.\n1273\t- **flow/saves**: records, trophies and the Hunt-Off autosave survive a reload (stubbed `E.store`); CONTINUE resumes at\n1274\t  the next hunt.\n1275\t\n1276\t### 9.3 Browser checks (`--browser`, Playwright, Chromium from the cache, `TMPDIR` set)\n1277\t- `tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and on deep links (`#title`, `#menu`, `#hunt/hollow/1`, `#hunt/bugle/2`,\n1278\t  `#hunt/muskeg/3`, `#trophy/muskeg`, `#bonus/crow`, `#range`, `#lodge`, `#about`, `#attract`, `#party/2`,\n1279\t  `#animallab`): no errors or warnings; screenshots saved to `tests/out/` (look at them: palettes, fog, readability,\n1280\t  HUD at 10 feet).\n1281\t- `--size 390x844@3` and a touch-only emulation: the title shows the message and the settings button.\n1282\t- **browser/pick**: the pick-agreement check (5.9).\n1283\t- **browser/glyphs**: a gamepad is emulated via `navigator.getGamepads` stub: prompts show PlayStation glyphs; after\n1284\t  switching the setting, Xbox; mouse movement switches prompts to mouse icons.\n1285\t- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs ... --seed 1`) of gaits, deaths, the Trophy Cam and banners: review by eye; these\n1286\t  are the only checks that need eyes.\n1287\t\n1288\t### 9.4 AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n1289\tCopy `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` next to a copy of the bundle in `tests/out/hub/`; start\n1290\t`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (record the PID and port); open\n1291\t`harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright; confirm the frames' title is \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\"; wait for\n1292\t`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`; require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; print failing checks. Repeat\n1293\twith `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and with `&scenario=host-leave`. Stop the server by its PID.\n1294\t\n1295\t### 9.5 Balance (`--balance`)\n1296\tRuns each site 20 times per bot skill (novice, average, expert) at different seeds and prints, per site: mean score,\n1297\tbucks bagged %, does shot, time used, accuracy. Targets: average bot bags 70-85% of bucks and scores near par; novice\n1298\t40-60%; expert above 95% with a clean sweep at least half the time. Set the hunts' par and the rivals' scores from\n1299\tthese numbers.\n1300\t\n1301\t---\n1302\t\n1303\t## 10. Definition of done (from TASK.md)\n1304\t- [ ] `BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174813.html` in the work root runs from `file://`,\n1305\t      single file, no network; dev files in the subfolder.\n1306\t- [ ] Every system in section 5 and all content in section 6 present; no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n1307\t- [ ] Engine native style (pixel art, E.tones shading, outlines, pixel font) and native animation (Humanoid, Blob,\n1308\t      and our procedural Quadruped in the same spirit); new art for animals, antlers and hunting props.\n1309\t- [ ] All music, sound and voices synthesized in code; gibberish voices.\n1310\t- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; KB+M native (mouse aims and clicks, hover focuses); prompts follow the last device;\n1311\t      PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; no dense web screens.\n1312\t- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, the attract mode runs.\n1313\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits.\n1314\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders (Appendix A), reset to defaults, and the tools.\n1315\t- [ ] Local 1-4 players; AI Hub ghost mode passing the harness (2 players; 4 with latency and loss; host leaving).\n1316\t- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` green, with the full scripted playthrough; browser checks and screenshots reviewed.\n1317\t- [ ] About & Credits screen, the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (parses as JSON) carry Source Information,\n1318\t      Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback (Appendix E).\n1319\t\n1320\t---\n1321\t\n1322\t## Appendix A. Dev sliders (defaults)\n1323\t\n1324\t| Key (`dev.*`) | Default | Range | What |\n1325\t|---|---|---|---|\n1326\t| animalSpeed | 1.0 | 0.25-2 | all animal speeds |\n1327\t| spook | 1.0 | 0-2 | fear from gunshots and impacts |\n1328\t| doeShare | 1.0 | 0-2 | how many does and fawns spawns include |\n1329\t| spawnRate | 1.0 | 0.5-2 | time between spawn waves |\n1330\t| siteTime | 1.0 | 0.3-3 | site time limits (x) |\n1331\t| reticleSpeed | 400 | 150-900 | pad reticle px/s |\n1332\t| assist | 0.65 | 0-1 | aim-assist friction factor (1 = none) |\n1333\t| magazine | 5 | 1-10 | rounds in the tube |\n1334\t| rackTime | 0.22 | 0-0.6 | pump time (s) |\n1335\t| reloadTime | 1.25 | 0.2-3 | empty-tube reload (s) |\n1336\t| scopeMag | 3.5 | 1.5-6 | scope magnification |\n1337\t| sway | 2.6 | 0-6 | scope sway amplitude (px) |\n1338\t| breath | 3.0 | 1-6 | hold-breath seconds |\n1339\t| calls | 2 | 0-5 | calls per site |\n1340\t| callFreeze | 1.4 | 0-4 | seconds animals stop on a call |\n1341\t| distanceSlope | 75 | 25-200 | metres per +1 distance multiplier |\n1342\t| heartMult / headMult / lungMult | 2.0 / 1.8 / 1.6 | 0.5-4 | zone multipliers |\n1343\t| runningMult | 1.25 | 1-2 | running-shot multiplier |\n1344\t| antlerBoost | 1.15 | 1-2 | antler drawing scale |\n1345\t| animalScale | 1.1 | 0.8-1.5 | arcade size boost for every animal (drawing and hit zones together) |\n1346\t| fog | 1.0 | 0-2 | fog density (look) |\n1347\t| timeOfDay | 0 | -1..1 | shifts the sun and grade (look) |\n1348\t| timeScale | 1.0 | 0.1-2 | game speed |\n1349\t\n1350\t## Appendix B. Data shapes\n1351\t\n1352\t```js\n1353\tdef('hunt', 'hollow', { name: 'Hollow Creek', species: 'whitetail', seed: 1101, palette: 'autumn-morning',\n1354\t  sun: { bearing: 95, elevation: 12, color: '#ffd8a0', ambient: '#6a7a9a' }, fog: { color: '#cdd6e0', near: 160, far: 900, mistTop: 6 },\n1355\t  backdrop: { sky: ['#8fb4e0', '#f0c8a0'], layers: [/* E.Backdrop layers */] }, weather: { kind: 'leaves', amount: .3 },\n1356\t  terrain: { base: { amp: 22, scale: 280, octaves: 5, warp: 45 }, features: [/* 5.2 */] },\n1357\t  scatter: [{ props: [['oak', .4], ['maple', .3], ['birch', .3]], spacing: 7, where: 'forest' }, /* ... */],\n1358\t  vantages: { creekStand: { at: [604, 556], eye: 4.5, yaw: 12, kind: 'treestand' }, /* ... */ },\n1359\t  trails: [['creekStand', 'fieldBlind', [[604, 556], [700, 610], [760, 640]]], /* ... */],\n1360\t  sites: ['hollow-1', 'hollow-2', 'hollow-3'], trophy: 'iron-rack', bonus: 'crow-patrol', par: 6000,\n1361\t  rivals: { earl: 3300, loretta: 5100, dwayne: 6000 }, ambience: 'hollow', voiceHost: 'granny' });\n1362\tdef('species', 'whitetail', { rig: 'deer', size: 1, speeds: [1.3, 3.4, 8.5], hp: 1, temper: .35, targets: ['buck'],\n1363\t  protected: ['doe', 'fawn'], antlers: { kind: 'typical', points: [4, 12] }, base: p => 100 + 15 * p, call: 'grunt' });\n1364\tdef('critter', 'skunk', { rig: 'blob', look: {...}, behavior: 'waddle', points: -100, protected: true, effect: 'stink' });\n1365\tdef('bonus', 'crow-patrol', { hunt: 'hollow', vantage: 'porch', time: 30, tube: 10, rack: .15, host: 'granny',\n1366\t  timeline: function* (B) { /* spawns targets on arcs */ }, targets: { crow: 100, golden: 500, hank: -250 } });\n1367\tdef('beat', 'iron-rack-legend', { lines: [['dub', 'Old Iron Rack. Fourteen points.', { pose: 'kneel' }], /* ... */] });\n1368\tdef('bark', 'doe', { lines: [\"DOE! YOU'RE OUT!\", \"THAT'S A DOE! HOLSTER UP!\", 'AW, NOT MAMA!'], priority: 3 });\n1369\t```\n1370\t\n1371\t## Appendix C. Engine changes (keep this list; it goes in the Engine Feedback)\n1372\t1. **New modules** `vista.js` (E.Lens, E.Heightfield, E.Vista, E.Impostors), `quadruped.js` (E.Quadruped,\n1373\t   E.Antlers), `babble.js` (E.Babble): general systems with engine-style headers (manual, API, rules), loaded after\n1374\t   the full engine. Why: the engine's floor views are flat and orthographic, Mode 7 is a flat floor, and it has no\n1375\t   four-legged rig or voice synth.\n1376\t2. **Default button symbols**: `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs.value = 'playstation'` (TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs by\n1377\t   default; the Xbox option stays in the same setting).\n1378\t3. **E.Shell**: custom screens accept `rows: [settingKeys]` (render `_row(k)` for each), and settings specs accept\n1379\t   `hidden: true` (left out of the standard Settings screen), for the dev mode's tuning rows.\n1380\t4. **Audio**: `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music')` returns the bus node for custom Web Audio graphs (Babble voices), and\n1381\t   `audio.echo({ delay, feedback, mix })` adds an echo send used by gunshots. Both headless-safe (null without a\n1382\t   context).\n1383\t5. Optional: wheel steps as bindable codes (`WheelDown`, `WheelUp`) so pump-on-wheel shows on the Controls screen.\n1384\t\n1385\t## Appendix D. `game.debug` and the snapshot\n1386\t\n1387\t```js\n1388\tgame.debug = {\n1389\t  snapshot() { return { scene, segment, mode, hunt, site, siteTime, attract, devOpen, paused: game.paused,\n1390\t    players: [{ n, device, score, mag, chambered, benched, scoped, breath, calls, reticle: [x, y] }],\n1391\t    actors: [{ id, kind, sex, state, x, y, z, hp, wounded, bagger, visible }], bucksLeft, results, stars,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"6169816c-95d6-48c7-ad74-994fcd2ee6a2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:54.346Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 7. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild the spine first, one hunt to a full vertical slice, then widen. Each milestone ends with its tests passing\n(`node tests/run.mjs`) and, where it says so, screenshots looked at.\n\n| # | Milestone | Delivers | Done when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Setup | dev folder, engine and hub copies, manifest, build script, dev page, test runner and headless loader, `game.debug` stub with snapshot | `node tests/run.mjs` runs (one smoke test); the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors |\n| M1 | Gallery on a flat floor | E.Lens, Vista with flat terrain, Backdrop sky, billboards with impostors (library trees and rocks), static deer silhouettes, P1 reticle (mouse and pad), fire with analytic sphere hits, a minimal HUD | shooting a silhouette works by mouse and pad; lens tests pass; screenshot looks like a pixel landscape |\n| M2 | The deer | E.Quadruped whitetail (skeleton, 4 gaits, poses, antlers, outline, LOD, zones, x-ray, mount), Animal Lab | quadruped tests pass; filmstrips of every gait and the death look right |\n| M3 | The land | E.Heightfield (base, features, water, ground types, light bake, scatter, occluders), terrain raster with occlusion, water, fog and mist, Hollow Creek map, custom props (corn, reeds, tall grass, birch, barn, stand, blind) | terrain and occlusion tests pass; Hollow's three vantages screenshot well; animals hide behind crests |\n| M4 | Shooting for real | rifle (pump, tube, reload), scope lens with sway and breath, call, aim assist, full shot resolution with zones, occluders, terrain and water, impacts and particles, scoring v1, banners and pops | weapon, aim, shot and score tests pass; pick-agreement check at 95% |\n| M5 | Living animals and sites | actors, orders, paths on terrain, herds, spooking, calls, wounds, death, patterns, the site runtime and director, Hollow sites 1-3, the tally and Shot Chart, walk-ins | ai and site flow tests pass; a person can play Hollow Creek's three sites start to finish |\n| M6 | Vertical slice | Old Iron Rack and the Trophy Cam, the bonus framework and Crow Patrol, hunt results with E.Arcade initials and ranks, records, the Lodge v1, story beats with portraits | the Hollow hunt plays from its card to its results; the slice playthrough test passes |\n| M7 | Sound and voice | songs, layers and stings, ambience beds, every sfx, gunshot echoes, E.Babble voices, barks and captions, the Sound Lab | every sound plays in the Sound Lab; barks fit on screen; headless runs stay silent |\n| M8 | Front end | title with logo and live vista, main menu and pages (UIKit), the Shell theme and help, settings, glyph prompts (PS default, Xbox option, KB+M), difficulty, the touch-only gate, the Practice Range | prompts, touch and menu flow tests pass; menus work with pad, keys and mouse hover |\n| M9 | Party | up to 4 local players: joining, colours and shapes, per-player rifles and HUD panels, benching, shared kills, the director-only camera, party tallies and podium, Quick Draw | party flow tests pass; two pads and a mouse play a hunt together |\n| M10 | Bugle Ridge and Muskeg Lake | elk and moose presets, canid and cow, the two maps, six sites, The Duke and Big Mo, Saucer Season and Snowball Standoff, all critters, the Hunt-Off campaign with rivals, autosave and ceremony | site tests pass for all 9 sites; the campaign playthrough test passes |\n| M11 | Attract and dev mode | the idle timer, the attract playlist and HunterBot, dev mode (Shell rows, sliders, reset, tools, overlays, free camera), deep links | attract and dev tests pass |\n| M12 | AI Hub | session flow, own card, the Hub Hunt-Off timeline, ghosts, reporting, end handling; the bundle with the session client first | hub stub tests pass; the harness passes with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5, and with `scenario=host-leave` |\n| M13 | Polish and balance | bot balance runs and tuning (pars, rivals, speeds, windows), look passes on every vantage (palettes, fog, props, lights), animation passes, About & Credits with the reports, `exit-interview.json`, final full test run | Definition of done (section 10) holds |\n\nKeep the game playable from M1 on; keep the full test command green after every milestone.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it matters | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **The custom renderer** (column terrain, occlusion of billboards, scope second pass) is slow or wrong | everything is seen through it | M1 ships it with a flat floor behind the final interfaces; M3 adds heights with unit tests for breakpoints and `occY` against brute force; screenshots per vantage. Fallback if hills fail: keep the flat floor and fake relief with Backdrop hill layers and big \"ridge\" billboards; the game logic doesn't change. Performance is out of scope, but keep it playable: typed arrays, no allocation per pixel, impostors, skip billboards fully hidden |\n| **Animals don't read** (deer at a distance look like blobs; bucks vs does unclear) | the core skill is telling bucks from does | the Animal Lab and filmstrips in M2; strong silhouettes, outlines, antlers always drawn with the readability boost, LOD that never drops antlers; screenshots at 20, 60, 120 and 200 m; the Antler glint assist |\n| **Hits don't match what you see** | unfair misses kill a shooting game | zones are built from the same joints that are drawn; dev overlay shows volumes and rays; the pick-agreement browser check (95%) every run |\n| **Gaits slide or pop** | broken animation ruins the look | hoof locking, a planted-hoof test, filmstrips per gait; tune speeds to strides |\n| **Hub ghost sync** (copies drift apart, spawns differ, protocol misses) | the hub drops games that fail its check | timeline keyed to `AIHub.time()`; cameras scripted; spawn RNG separate from cosmetics; a headless hub stub test; the real harness in M12 with latency and loss; build-time check of the client and metas |\n| **Input breadth** (mouse absolute vs stick velocity, up to 4 players, prompts by device, glyph defaults, menus by hover) | 10-foot and KB+M must both feel native | one InputRouter per player tested headless with `input.press`, `input.feed` and pad codes; the Range teaches every control with live glyphs |\n| **Audio that sounds cheap** | gunshots and calls sell the fantasy | layered voices with echoes; the Sound Lab for quick iteration; volume balance pass in M13 |\n| **Content volume** (9 sites, 3 trophies, 3 bonus games, range) | time | data-driven sites and patterns, one hunt fully done before the others, the dev free camera's bearing/distance readout for authoring, the bot for quick runs |\n| **Engine assumptions** (overlay drawing bypasses engine lighting, particles, weather, camera; HTML shell over the canvas) | surprises late | own fx, weather and grade from M1; check that the pause menu, settings and corner draw over our overlay in M1 |\n| **Bundle mistakes** (client not first or edited, missing metas, network calls) | hub rejection, broken file | build-time assertions (3.5); tests run against the bundle as well as the dev page |\n| **Touch-only false positives** (touch laptops) | blocks real players | needs coarse pointer and no fine pointer; cleared by any key, mouse or pad input |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing\n\n### 9.1 One command\n`node tests/run.mjs` runs every headless suite (unit and flow) in Node with the engine headless (`new E.Game()` has no\nDOM there; `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact 1/120 s steps; `input.tap`, `hold`, `press`, `feed` drive it;\n`game.debug.snapshot()` reads it). It prints **only failures** and one line: `214 passed, 0 failed (41.2 s)`; exit code 1\non any failure. `node tests/run.mjs <filter>` runs matching suites only: rerun a suite only after changing the code it\ncovers. Flags: `--browser` adds the Playwright checks (9.3), `--hub` the harness (9.4), `--balance` the bot statistics\n(9.5, prints a table; not pass/fail). Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit; the tests and\nyour own looks at screenshots decide.\n\nThe loader (`tests/lib/load.mjs`) builds a `vm` context with stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location` with\na hash, `matchMedia`, `navigator`, optional `AIHub` stub), loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, the new modules, the asset set\nand `src/*.js` in manifest order, and returns `{ E, game, D: game.debug, step, tap, hold, press, feed, until }`. A\nsecond loader extracts the scripts from the built HTML so the bundle itself is smoke-tested.\n\n### 9.2 Suites (headless)\n- **unit/lens, unit/terrain, unit/vista, unit/quadruped, unit/ai, unit/weapon, unit/aim, unit/shot, unit/score,\n  unit/prompts**: as listed in each system above.\n- **unit/lint**: no `Math.random` in gameplay files; no TODO-like markers or placeholder text; every registered site,\n  trophy, bonus, critter, beat and bark id referenced exists; every bark and caption fits the screen at its scale.\n- **flow/sites**: every site at seeds 1-3 with the cheat bot (clean sweep, early end) and with no shots (time out,\n  escapes); doe benching; protected critter penalties.\n- **flow/playthrough** (the scripted playthrough of the whole game): title -> PRESS START -> menu -> HUNT-OFF ->\n  for each hunt: intro dialog skipped -> 3 sites with the average bot -> tallies -> trophy (cheat bot bags it; Trophy\n  Cam runs and time scale returns to 1) -> bonus -> results with initials entered -> next hunt (autosave written) ->\n  ceremony -> Lodge shows 3 trophy mounts -> About pages -> title. Checks at each step through the snapshot; no errors\n  (`game.errors` empty); total under 30 simulated minutes.\n- **flow/modes**: Single Hunt for each hunt; Bonus Only for each game; Practice Range with scripted inputs completing\n  every station; Party with 2 and 4 bots; Quick Draw.\n- **flow/attract**: 10 s idle on the title starts the attract mode; it cycles through its playlist (snapshot shows each\n  clip); a key, a mouse move, a pad button each return to the title.\n- **flow/dev**: 5.22's checks.\n- **flow/touch**: 5.25's checks.\n- **flow/hub**: 5.26's checks with the stub.\n- **flow/determinism**: the same seed and scripted inputs twice give the same `stateHash` after 60 s of a site; a run\n  with extra cosmetic RNG draws gives the same spawn log.\n- **flow/saves**: records, trophies and the Hunt-Off autosave survive a reload (stubbed `E.store`); CONTINUE resumes at\n  the next hunt.\n\n### 9.3 Browser checks (`--browser`, Playwright, Chromium from the cache, `TMPDIR` set)\n- `tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and on deep links (`#title`, `#menu`, `#hunt/hollow/1`, `#hunt/bugle/2`,\n  `#hunt/muskeg/3`, `#trophy/muskeg`, `#bonus/crow`, `#range`, `#lodge`, `#about`, `#attract`, `#party/2`,\n  `#animallab`): no errors or warnings; screenshots saved to `tests/out/` (look at them: palettes, fog, readability,\n  HUD at 10 feet).\n- `--size 390x844@3` and a touch-only emulation: the title shows the message and the settings button.\n- **browser/pick**: the pick-agreement check (5.9).\n- **browser/glyphs**: a gamepad is emulated via `navigator.getGamepads` stub: prompts show PlayStation glyphs; after\n  switching the setting, Xbox; mouse movement switches prompts to mouse icons.\n- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs ... --seed 1`) of gaits, deaths, the Trophy Cam and banners: review by eye; these\n  are the only checks that need eyes.\n\n### 9.4 AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\nCopy `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` next to a copy of the bundle in `tests/out/hub/`; start\n`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (record the PID and port); open\n`harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright; confirm the frames' title is \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\"; wait for\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`; require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; print failing checks. Repeat\nwith `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and with `&scenario=host-leave`. Stop the server by its PID.\n\n### 9.5 Balance (`--balance`)\nRuns each site 20 times per bot skill (novice, average, expert) at different seeds and prints, per site: mean score,\nbucks bagged %, does shot, time used, accuracy. Targets: average bot bags 70-85% of bucks and scores near par; novice\n40-60%; expert above 95% with a clean sweep at least half the time. Set the hunts' par and the rivals' scores from\nthese numbers.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Definition of done (from TASK.md)\n- [ ] `BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174813.html` in the work root runs from `file://`,\n      single file, no network; dev files in the subfolder.\n- [ ] Every system in section 5 and all content in section 6 present; no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- [ ] Engine native style (pixel art, E.tones shading, outlines, pixel font) and native animation (Humanoid, Blob,\n      and our procedural Quadruped in the same spirit); new art for animals, antlers and hunting props.\n- [ ] All music, sound and voices synthesized in code; gibberish voices.\n- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; KB+M native (mouse aims and clicks, hover focuses); prompts follow the last device;\n      PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; no dense web screens.\n- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, the attract mode runs.\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders (Appendix A), reset to defaults, and the tools.\n- [ ] Local 1-4 players; AI Hub ghost mode passing the harness (2 players; 4 with latency and loss; host leaving).\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` green, with the full scripted playthrough; browser checks and screenshots reviewed.\n- [ ] About & Credits screen, the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (parses as JSON) carry Source Information,\n      Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback (Appendix E).\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A. Dev sliders (defaults)\n\n| Key (`dev.*`) | Default | Range | What |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| animalSpeed | 1.0 | 0.25-2 | all animal speeds |\n| spook | 1.0 | 0-2 | fear from gunshots and impacts |\n| doeShare | 1.0 | 0-2 | how many does and fawns spawns include |\n| spawnRate | 1.0 | 0.5-2 | time between spawn waves |\n| siteTime | 1.0 | 0.3-3 | site time limits (x) |\n| reticleSpeed | 400 | 150-900 | pad reticle px/s |\n| assist | 0.65 | 0-1 | aim-assist friction factor (1 = none) |\n| magazine | 5 | 1-10 | rounds in the tube |\n| rackTime | 0.22 | 0-0.6 | pump time (s) |\n| reloadTime | 1.25 | 0.2-3 | empty-tube reload (s) |\n| scopeMag | 3.5 | 1.5-6 | scope magnification |\n| sway | 2.6 | 0-6 | scope sway amplitude (px) |\n| breath | 3.0 | 1-6 | hold-breath seconds |\n| calls | 2 | 0-5 | calls per site |\n| callFreeze | 1.4 | 0-4 | seconds animals stop on a call |\n| distanceSlope | 75 | 25-200 | metres per +1 distance multiplier |\n| heartMult / headMult / lungMult | 2.0 / 1.8 / 1.6 | 0.5-4 | zone multipliers |\n| runningMult | 1.25 | 1-2 | running-shot multiplier |\n| antlerBoost | 1.15 | 1-2 | antler drawing scale |\n| animalScale | 1.1 | 0.8-1.5 | arcade size boost for every animal (drawing and hit zones together) |\n| fog | 1.0 | 0-2 | fog density (look) |\n| timeOfDay | 0 | -1..1 | shifts the sun and grade (look) |\n| timeScale | 1.0 | 0.1-2 | game speed |\n\n## Appendix B. Data shapes\n\n```js\ndef('hunt', 'hollow', { name: 'Hollow Creek', species: 'whitetail', seed: 1101, palette: 'autumn-morning',\n  sun: { bearing: 95, elevation: 12, color: '#ffd8a0', ambient: '#6a7a9a' }, fog: { color: '#cdd6e0', near: 160, far: 900, mistTop: 6 },\n  backdrop: { sky: ['#8fb4e0', '#f0c8a0'], layers: [/* E.Backdrop layers */] }, weather: { kind: 'leaves', amount: .3 },\n  terrain: { base: { amp: 22, scale: 280, octaves: 5, warp: 45 }, features: [/* 5.2 */] },\n  scatter: [{ props: [['oak', .4], ['maple', .3], ['birch', .3]], spacing: 7, where: 'forest' }, /* ... */],\n  vantages: { creekStand: { at: [604, 556], eye: 4.5, yaw: 12, kind: 'treestand' }, /* ... */ },\n  trails: [['creekStand', 'fieldBlind', [[604, 556], [700, 610], [760, 640]]], /* ... */],\n  sites: ['hollow-1', 'hollow-2', 'hollow-3'], trophy: 'iron-rack', bonus: 'crow-patrol', par: 6000,\n  rivals: { earl: 3300, loretta: 5100, dwayne: 6000 }, ambience: 'hollow', voiceHost: 'granny' });\ndef('species', 'whitetail', { rig: 'deer', size: 1, speeds: [1.3, 3.4, 8.5], hp: 1, temper: .35, targets: ['buck'],\n  protected: ['doe', 'fawn'], antlers: { kind: 'typical', points: [4, 12] }, base: p => 100 + 15 * p, call: 'grunt' });\ndef('critter', 'skunk', { rig: 'blob', look: {...}, behavior: 'waddle', points: -100, protected: true, effect: 'stink' });\ndef('bonus', 'crow-patrol', { hunt: 'hollow', vantage: 'porch', time: 30, tube: 10, rack: .15, host: 'granny',\n  timeline: function* (B) { /* spawns targets on arcs */ }, targets: { crow: 100, golden: 500, hank: -250 } });\ndef('beat', 'iron-rack-legend', { lines: [['dub', 'Old Iron Rack. Fourteen points.', { pose: 'kneel' }], /* ... */] });\ndef('bark', 'doe', { lines: [\"DOE! YOU'RE OUT!\", \"THAT'S A DOE! HOLSTER UP!\", 'AW, NOT MAMA!'], priority: 3 });\n```\n\n## Appendix C. Engine changes (keep this list; it goes in the Engine Feedback)\n1. **New modules** `vista.js` (E.Lens, E.Heightfield, E.Vista, E.Impostors), `quadruped.js` (E.Quadruped,\n   E.Antlers), `babble.js` (E.Babble): general systems with engine-style headers (manual, API, rules), loaded after\n   the full engine. Why: the engine's floor views are flat and orthographic, Mode 7 is a flat floor, and it has no\n   four-legged rig or voice synth.\n2. **Default button symbols**: `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs.value = 'playstation'` (TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs by\n   default; the Xbox option stays in the same setting).\n3. **E.Shell**: custom screens accept `rows: [settingKeys]` (render `_row(k)` for each), and settings specs accept\n   `hidden: true` (left out of the standard Settings screen), for the dev mode's tuning rows.\n4. **Audio**: `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music')` returns the bus node for custom Web Audio graphs (Babble voices), and\n   `audio.echo({ delay, feedback, mix })` adds an echo send used by gunshots. Both headless-safe (null without a\n   context).\n5. Optional: wheel steps as bindable codes (`WheelDown`, `WheelUp`) so pump-on-wheel shows on the Controls screen.\n\n## Appendix D. `game.debug` and the snapshot\n\n```js\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot() { return { scene, segment, mode, hunt, site, siteTime, attract, devOpen, paused: game.paused,\n    players: [{ n, device, score, mag, chambered, benched, scoped, breath, calls, reticle: [x, y] }],\n    actors: [{ id, kind, sex, state, x, y, z, hp, wounded, bagger, visible }], bucksLeft, results, stars,","numLines":200,"startLine":1192,"totalLines":1423}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TyYrzQB4enLmGrsscsGpXM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
