{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh29U3X9hBGnebhD96GF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `PLAN.md` in this folder; nothing is built yet. The game is **Big Buck Hunt-Off**: I brainstormed 50 riffs on the source's name and a cryptographic random pick chose #33.\n\n- **The game:** an arcade light-gun hunting shooter seen in first person, with the camera moving on fixed rails over a 3D-looking pixel landscape. Hills and fog hide the animals. The core rules:\n  - Shoot bucks only; shoot a doe and you sit out the rest of that site.\n  - Pump after every shot.\n  - Every animal has real hit zones, and after each site an x-ray card shows where each shot landed.\n  - A scope with sway and a hold-breath button handles long shots.\n  - A deer, elk or moose call makes animals stop and look for a moment.\n- **Content:** three hunts (whitetail deer, elk, moose), each with three sites, a named trophy animal and a silly bonus round, about 17 minutes for the full campaign. Around that:\n  - 12 small critters for bonus points, some protected (a skunk, a cow, an eagle).\n  - A practice range that works as the tutorial.\n  - A trophy room and a campaign against rival hunters.\n  - A folksy cast with all-caps announcer calls and gibberish voices.\n- **Players:** 1 to 4 on one screen, and AI Hub online play in ghost mode. That's a 3-minute timed round where everyone gets the same seeded hunt, sees the others' crosshairs and keeps their own score.\n- **Tech:** built on the engine's handoff package, plus three new engine modules: the terrain renderer, a four-legged animal rig and the voice synth. It also makes small engine changes, all listed in the plan; one of them makes PlayStation button symbols the default, as the task asks.\n- **Build order:** 14 milestones, finishing the deer hunt end to end before the other two.\n- **Biggest risk:** the custom renderer. To reduce it, a flat-ground version ships first behind the final interfaces.\n- **Testing:**\n  - One command, `node tests/run.mjs`, covers every part of the game, including a full scripted playthrough by a bot player.\n  - Browser checks confirm that hits match what is drawn on screen.\n  - The AI Hub's own test harness must pass with 2 and 4 players.\n\nTwo notes:\n- **`/tmp` is full** on this machine (a shared ramdisk at 100%). My first download failed there, and Claude Code keeps its temp files there too. The plan tells the builders to point their temp folder at the dev folder.\n- **Research copies:** I left copies of the engine and the hub library in `~/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research` for the builders to reuse. Delete it whenever you like.\n\nSources: [Big Buck Hunter (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Buck_Hunter), [Giant Bomb](https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-22443/), [MobyGames](https://www.mobygames.com/game/wii/big-buck-hunter-pro), [Macworld](https://www.macworld.com/article/1144021/bigbuckhunterreview.html), [Raw Thrills listing](https://mpamusement.com/collections/video-games/products/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-shooting-game), [Big Buck Hunter Reloaded change log](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fqWR3bvlkIrAa-nVDMO4MPC2EuG-U5Sm9P8Pve_QNMk/mobilebasic), [Supercheats](https://www.supercheats.com/xbox360/bigbuckhunterpro.htm)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":484476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"015807a2-2644-4792-b144-44c146547830","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:29:03.888Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh29TnebTiPCXoLmWvCH"}
