{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hssq9To2yZ1iC9xXecUAbw","type":"tool_result","content":"**Manufacturer and release**\n- Made by Raw Thrills, released in 2005 (product database).\n- Category: \"Shooting Games,\" style \"Gun Shooting Games.\"\n\n**Guns and controls**\n- Includes \"two standard guns for multiplayer gameplay.\"\n- Controller type is \"Gun,\" with \"Standard\" force feedback.\n- The page does not say whether the guns are pump action.\n\n**Players and game modes**\n- Supports 2 players.\n- Listed gameplay modes: Single Play, Versus Play, and Co-operative Play.\n- A new two-player mode called \"Shootout\" lets two players \"compete in head-to-head competition.\"\n\n**Animals**\n- Features 5 \"high-definition 3D modeled animals\" to hunt.\n- Named species: Whitetail Deer, Elk, Pronghorn Antelope, Moose, and Bighorn Sheep.\n- Hunts are organized by species rather than region.\n\n**Critters**\n- Critters appear alongside the main game animals and can be shot for bonus points.\n- Listed critters: mountain lions, raccoons, possums, skunks, blackbirds, bluebirds, squirrels, foxes, wolves, and rabbits.\n- The page says critters \"can help a player's score dramatically.\"\n\n**Bonus rounds**\n- Includes 15 \"improved and new\" bonus rounds, accessible through regular play or a \"Bonus Only\" purchase option.\n- Named rounds include Duck Hunt, Pappy's Moonshine Bonus, Pie in the Sky Bonus, Boars Gone Wild, Mug Shot Bonus, and Turkey Hunt Bonus, among others.\n\n**Other facts**\n- Screen: horizontal, 1080p (1920x1080).\n- Dimensions: 137.2 cm wide, 76.2 cm deep, 127.0 cm high.\n- Linking: listed as \"No.\"\n\n**Not mentioned on the page**\n- Shooting female animals.\n- Scoring details beyond critter bonus points.\n- Tournaments or online features."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"8c97ba2e-d48b-4a9f-a011-7f9d727dfaa8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:16.440Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":26831,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Manufacturer and release**\n- Made by Raw Thrills, released in 2005 (product database).\n- Category: \"Shooting Games,\" style \"Gun Shooting Games.\"\n\n**Guns and controls**\n- Includes \"two standard guns for multiplayer gameplay.\"\n- Controller type is \"Gun,\" with \"Standard\" force feedback.\n- The page does not say whether the guns are pump action.\n\n**Players and game modes**\n- Supports 2 players.\n- Listed gameplay modes: Single Play, Versus Play, and Co-operative Play.\n- A new two-player mode called \"Shootout\" lets two players \"compete in head-to-head competition.\"\n\n**Animals**\n- Features 5 \"high-definition 3D modeled animals\" to hunt.\n- Named species: Whitetail Deer, Elk, Pronghorn Antelope, Moose, and Bighorn Sheep.\n- Hunts are organized by species rather than region.\n\n**Critters**\n- Critters appear alongside the main game animals and can be shot for bonus points.\n- Listed critters: mountain lions, raccoons, possums, skunks, blackbirds, bluebirds, squirrels, foxes, wolves, and rabbits.\n- The page says critters \"can help a player's score dramatically.\"\n\n**Bonus rounds**\n- Includes 15 \"improved and new\" bonus rounds, accessible through regular play or a \"Bonus Only\" purchase option.\n- Named rounds include Duck Hunt, Pappy's Moonshine Bonus, Pie in the Sky Bonus, Boars Gone Wild, Mug Shot Bonus, and Turkey Hunt Bonus, among others.\n\n**Other facts**\n- Screen: horizontal, 1080p (1920x1080).\n- Dimensions: 137.2 cm wide, 76.2 cm deep, 127.0 cm high.\n- Linking: listed as \"No.\"\n\n**Not mentioned on the page**\n- Shooting female animals.\n- Scoring details beyond critter bonus points.\n- Tournaments or online features.","durationMs":6688,"url":"https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/big-buck-hunter-pro-arcade-machine-9210/"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hssq9To2yZ1iC9xXecUAbw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R95UkvtwMaXqiSgZWeRcav","type":"tool_result","content":"**Gameplay rules**\n- Each scene opens with animals grazing until a few seconds pass or the first shot is fired, then they bolt.\n- Bucks and does both cross the screen. You tap where you want to fire.\n- The reviewer says the game expects you to \"lead\" targets by firing slightly in front of them.\n- A buck dies from one well-placed shot to the vitals or two shots anywhere on the body.\n- Hitting a doe ends the scene with no further scoring, though bucks already taken still count.\n- Each scene has three bucks, often accompanied by a doe.\n\n**Reloading**\n- The reload button sits at the bottom of the screen and must be tapped after every shot.\n- The reviewer found that holding the phone flat and using one hand to fire and reload gave the best accuracy.\n\n**Scoring**\n- A scoring screen shows where shots landed on the target after each scene.\n- Points depend on factors such as rack points, animal size and distance, and bonus critters.\n\n**Bonus rounds and critters**\n- Finishing a hunting site unlocks one of three bonus areas: ducks taking off vertically, gophers popping out of the dirt, and frogs on lily pads.\n- The frog round is described as \"almost comically simple,\" with the reviewer noting that anything short of a perfect 10 out of 10 is a sign of poor aim.\n- Birds, squirrels, and coyotes can be shot as bonus critters.\n\n**Modes and sites**\n- There are three wooded hunting sites: two green and one snowy.\n- The app includes a locator that finds nearby arcade units via Google Maps, plus networked and local scoreboards.\n\n**Comparison with the arcade version**\n- The reviewer says the arcade version gives a clearer sense of where shots will land, while touchscreen aiming is less reliable, which is the reviewer's main complaint.\n\n**Tone**\n- The review is playful and jokey. Examples include the gopher bonus being introduced with \"Freeze, gopher!\" and a quip about cutting back on the gin."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941","uuid":"6aabbe4e-487d-4dc1-9913-ea8afeae1e99","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:18.723Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":252174,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Gameplay rules**\n- Each scene opens with animals grazing until a few seconds pass or the first shot is fired, then they bolt.\n- Bucks and does both cross the screen. You tap where you want to fire.\n- The reviewer says the game expects you to \"lead\" targets by firing slightly in front of them.\n- A buck dies from one well-placed shot to the vitals or two shots anywhere on the body.\n- Hitting a doe ends the scene with no further scoring, though bucks already taken still count.\n- Each scene has three bucks, often accompanied by a doe.\n\n**Reloading**\n- The reload button sits at the bottom of the screen and must be tapped after every shot.\n- The reviewer found that holding the phone flat and using one hand to fire and reload gave the best accuracy.\n\n**Scoring**\n- A scoring screen shows where shots landed on the target after each scene.\n- Points depend on factors such as rack points, animal size and distance, and bonus critters.\n\n**Bonus rounds and critters**\n- Finishing a hunting site unlocks one of three bonus areas: ducks taking off vertically, gophers popping out of the dirt, and frogs on lily pads.\n- The frog round is described as \"almost comically simple,\" with the reviewer noting that anything short of a perfect 10 out of 10 is a sign of poor aim.\n- Birds, squirrels, and coyotes can be shot as bonus critters.\n\n**Modes and sites**\n- There are three wooded hunting sites: two green and one snowy.\n- The app includes a locator that finds nearby arcade units via Google Maps, plus networked and local scoreboards.\n\n**Comparison with the arcade version**\n- The reviewer says the arcade version gives a clearer sense of where shots will land, while touchscreen aiming is less reliable, which is the reviewer's main complaint.\n\n**Tone**\n- The review is playful and jokey. Examples include the gopher bonus being introduced with \"Freeze, gopher!\" and a quip about cutting back on the gin.","durationMs":7670,"url":"https://www.macworld.com/article/1144021/bigbuckhunterreview.html"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R95UkvtwMaXqiSgZWeRcav","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
