hinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"130646ee-9079-4003-b7bc-5ed0fe65fcad\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":38,"oldLines":23,"newStart":38,"newLines":30,"lines":[" "," ### 1.1 What research confirmed about Big Buck Hunter Pro"," ","-Research done while planning: Wikipedia's Big Buck Hunter article and web search results (Giant Bomb, MobyGames and","-retailer listings, quoted in search summaries; Giant Bomb and TV Tropes pages could not be fetched). Write \"unknown\"","-in the reports for anything below that is not listed as confirmed.","-","-- Arcade, released January 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, produced and distributed by Raw Thrills. Confirmed.","-- A two-gun cabinet with head-to-head play; the guns are pump-action (\"pump to reload\" is a speech call). Confirmed.","-- Shoot the males (bucks, bulls) as they run across the screen; a player who shoots a female is out until the next","-  site. Confirmed.","-- A hunt is split into five sites called treks, and a bonus round ends the session; a round ends when every male is","-  shot or some escape. Confirmed.","-- Points depend on distance, the animal's weight and accuracy. Bucks go down to a head shot, a heart shot, or by being","-  \"peppered\". Confirmed.","-- About 5 huntable animals, 15 bonus rounds and 12 critters that appear alongside the main animals for bonus points","-  (squirrels, rabbits, possums, skunks, raccoons, foxes, mountain lions, birds; sources disagree). Hunts are grouped by","-  animal (\"Whitetail Adventure\", \"Elk Adventure\"). Monthly national tournaments. Confirmed in part.","-- Tone: folksy, tongue-in-cheek rural humor with goofy bonus rounds and loud announcer calls. Confirmed in spirit","-  (bonus round names found); exact announcer lines are unknown.","+Research done while planning, on 2026-11-03: pages read directly were Wikipedia's \"Big Buck Hunter\" article, the","+Highway Games product listing for the Big Buck Hunter Pro cabinet, and Macworld's review of the iPhone port. Giant","+Bomb, TV Tropes, MobyGames and the Sinden wiki refused the fetch (HTTP 403) and one retailer page was rate-limited","+(HTTP 429); for those, only search-result summaries were seen. **Confirmed** below means read on a fetched page;","+**reported** means seen only in search summaries; **unknown** means not found. Use \"unknown\" in the reports for","+anything not confirmed.","+","+| Fact | Status | Where |","+|---|---|---|","+| Arcade game designed by Play Mechanix, produced and distributed by Raw Thrills; released January 23, 2006 (a retailer database lists 2005) | confirmed | Wikipedia; Highway Games |","+| Two guns on one cabinet; 1-2 players; single, versus and co-operative play, plus a head-to-head \"Shootout\" mode | confirmed | Wikipedia; Highway Games |","+| Shoot the males as they cross the screen; a player who shoots a female is out (the iPhone port: hitting a doe ends the scene, bucks already taken still count) | confirmed | Wikipedia; Macworld |","+| A hunt is split into five screens called treks, and a bonus round ends the session; a round ends when all males are shot or some escape | confirmed | Wikipedia |","+| Points depend on distance, the animal's weight or size, rack points, accuracy and bonus critters | confirmed | Wikipedia; Macworld |","+| A buck dies to one shot in the vitals or two anywhere on the body; after each scene a screen shows where the shots landed (the iPhone port) | confirmed | Macworld |","+| Animals graze until a few seconds pass or the first shot, then bolt; each scene has three bucks, often with a doe (the iPhone port) | confirmed | Macworld |","+| Five huntable animals: whitetail deer, elk, pronghorn antelope, moose, bighorn sheep; hunts organized by species, not region | confirmed | Highway Games |","+| Critters for bonus points: mountain lions, raccoons, possums, skunks, blackbirds, bluebirds, squirrels, foxes, wolves, rabbits | confirmed | Highway Games |","+| 15 bonus rounds, also sold as \"Bonus Only\" (named: Duck Hunt, Pappy's Moonshine, Pie in the Sky, Boars Gone Wild, Mug Shot, Turkey Hunt) | confirmed | Highway Games |","+| Monthly national tournaments | confirmed | Wikipedia |","+| Pump-action guns (\"pump to reload\" speech call) | reported | search summary of a Big Buck Hunter Reloaded change log; the iPhone port reloads after every shot (Macworld, confirmed) |","+| Head shots, heart shots, or \"peppering\" a buck | reported | search summary of Giant Bomb |","+| Tone: playful, jokey (the review's \"Freeze, gopher!\"), rural humor in the bonus round names | confirmed in spirit | Macworld; Highway Games |","+| The announcer's exact lines, the cabinet's art and music | unknown | (not researched on purpose: we don't copy them) |"," "," ### 1.2 Distinctive elements, turned into our mechanics"," "]},{"oldStart":64,"oldLines":7,"newStart":71,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Bucks only, a doe puts you out | Bucks/bulls are targets; does, fawns and calves are protected. Classic rule: shoot one and you're benched for the site (a Casual setting turns it into a points penalty) |"," | Sites (treks) and a bonus round | 3 hunts, each with 3 sites, a legendary **Trophy** encounter and a bonus game, all on one landscape per hunt with walk-in camera moves between vantages |"," | Distance, weight and accuracy scoring | Points = species base (from antler size) × distance × hit zone × running bonus, plus accuracy, clean sweep and critter bonuses |","-| Head and heart shots | Real 3D hit zones on every animal (heart, lungs, head, neck, shoulder, gut, ham, legs, antlers), shown afterwards on an **x-ray Shot Chart** |","+| Head and heart shots; a screen showing where shots landed | Real 3D hit zones on every animal (heart, lungs, head, neck, shoulder, gut, ham, legs, antlers), shown afterwards on our own **x-ray Shot Chart** |"," | Critters for bonus points | 12 critter designs across the hunts; some protected (skunk, Bessie the cow, eagle, loons) with comic penalties |"," | Goofy bonus rounds | Crow Patrol, Saucer Season, Snowball Standoff (ours) |"," | Tournaments | The Hunt-Off campaign against rival regulars; AI Hub rounds as an online Hunt-Off |"]},{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":7,"newStart":87,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," ### 1.4 Do not copy"," No names, logos, characters, art, music, sounds, bonus-round concepts, levels or look from Big Buck Hunter. Our title,","-cast, hunting grounds, bonus games, writing and art are our own. Reticle colors are the AI Hub seat colors (red, blue,","+cast, hunting grounds, bonus games, writing and art are our own. Whitetail deer, elk and moose are real animals every","+hunting game shares (the source also had pronghorn and bighorn sheep); our hunts, sites, trophies and critter roles","+are original, and none of our bonus games matches the source's named rounds. Reticle colors are the AI Hub seat colors (red, blue,"," green, gold), not the cabinet's gun colors. No gore: hits throw puffs of fur and dust; animals fold up and lie down."," "," ---"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1633,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1633,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":13900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"2ffbcf8e-5038-4e1f-b1a3-3b591d395553\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":14050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"c4977c7b-8861-4c27-a946-444d7f0c16e5\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":14200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"13966739-a745-45d8-883e-f2c8ab2cac3d\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":14400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"8576a872-dceb-495a-85f5-9623385ee618\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/work/PLAN.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X1CmYiQ2PMfLCRxJFrkKu4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
