Appendix E. The reports","-At the end the builders write, from what actually happened (not from this plan's hopes):","-- **Source Information** (chat reply, About screen, `exit-interview.json`): Date `2026-11-03 17:48:13`; Source \"Big Buck","-  Hunter Pro (Play Mechanix / Raw Thrills arcade, 2006)\"; Plan \"PLAN.md\"; Genre and Perspective (section 0); Tech","-  (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff with the new modules, vanilla JS, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0, Node 24 and Playwright","-  1.63 for tests); Art Direction; Animation; Audio; Online (AI Hub ghost mode); Testing (what was allowed and run);","-  Research (the planning research in 1.1 plus anything the builders add); Environment (\"Claude Code CLI (headless);","-  Linux; browser unknown\" or what is true); Model; Usage (estimates only if available, else \"unknown\").","-- **Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback**: answers to TASK.md's questions, in order.","-- **exit-interview.json** in the work root, beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape; check it parses","-  (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`). Suggested `aiHub` values:","-  name \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\"; tagline \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\"; description \"An arcade light-gun hunting","-  shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or","-  online.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Shooter\"; source \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\"; series \"Big Buck Hunter\"; players \"1–4\";","-  controls \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call:","-  Q or Triangle\"; tags [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"].","+## Appendix E. The reports: Source Information, feedback, the exit interview","+","+TASK.md requires Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the final chat reply and","+on the in-game About & Credits screen (5.27), and `exit-interview.json` in the work root beside the HTML. Every value is","+either confirmed or \"unknown\". The builders check every row below against what actually happened and update it; the","+values here are what is known at planning time.","+","+### E.1 Source Information","+","+| Field | Value at planning time | Builders |","+|---|---|---|","+| Date | 2026-11-03 17:48:13 | keep (TASK.md's) |","+| Source | Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills): confirmed (1.1) | keep |","+| Plan | PLAN.md (the planning stage itself had no plan: \"none\") | keep \"PLAN.md\" |","+| Genre and Perspective | genre and perspective as in section 0 | update if anything changed |","+| Tech | my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (full engine) with new modules `vista.js`, `quadruped.js`, `babble.js`; vanilla JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests on Node 24 (headless `vm`) and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium | update to the versions actually used |","+| Art Direction | the engine's native pixel style at 480 x 270; new procedural animals, antlers, hunting props; library trees, rocks, generic props | confirm |","+| Animation | engine-native procedural rigs: E.Humanoid (people), E.Blob (critters), new E.Quadruped (four-legged animals) | confirm |","+| Audio | all synthesized in code: chiptune songs, layered sfx with echoes, ambience, gibberish voices | confirm |","+| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players | confirm, and say whether the harness passed |","+| Testing | allowed: as TASK.md's Testing paragraph (unlimited headless tests, one command, scripted playthrough, screenshots only where scripts can't check, no subagent reviews); run so far: none (nothing is built yet) | replace \"run so far\" with what ran and its results |","+| Research | planning: Wikipedia, the Highway Games listing and Macworld's review read directly; Giant Bomb, TV Tropes, MobyGames and the Sinden wiki refused the fetch (403), a retailer page was rate-limited (429): search summaries only; engine handoff and AI Hub docs | add the builders' own research, or keep as is |","+| Environment | Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown | name the browser if one was used (Playwright Chromium for checks) |","+| Model | planning: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max | the builders' own model and effort |","+| Usage | unknown (no estimate is available at planning time) | an estimate if one is available, else \"unknown\" |","+","+### E.2 Feedback","+The builders answer TASK.md's questions from their own build, in order: Testing Feedback (how many issues testing","+caught; how many were critical or game-breaking; the most helpful test; the least helpful test), Engine Feedback (what","+they liked most; where they got stuck or guessed wrong; the most important thing they built themselves; the hardest","+part of using the engine; what they changed in the engine and why: start from Appendix C; the one thing they'd change),","+Prompt Feedback (what they liked most; what was confusing; the hardest thing; what they'd change). At planning time","+every one of these is \"unknown\": nothing has been built or tested.","+","+### E.3 exit-interview.json","+Exactly TASK.md's shape. Here it is filled with the planning-time values (it parses as JSON); the builders replace each","+\"unknown\" they can confirm (model, usage, the feedback answers) and update the other values to what actually shipped,","+then save it in the work root beside the HTML and check it parses:","+`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json', 'utf8'))\"`.","+","+```json","+{","+  \"sourceInformation\": {","+    \"date\": \"2026-11-03 17:48:13\",","+    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",","+    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",","+    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus and bonus mini-games\",","+    \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion bullet cam on trophy kills; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and Lodge\",","+    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (full engine) with new modules vista.js, quadruped.js and babble.js; vanilla JavaScript, Canvas 2D and Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 headless tests; Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium\",","+    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel style (PS1/N64-era 2D) at 480x270, with new procedural animals, antlers and hunting props, and library trees, rocks and generic props\",","+    \"animation\": \"The engine's native procedural rigs posed by math every step: E.Humanoid for people, E.Blob for small critters, and a new procedural E.Quadruped for deer, elk, moose, canids and the cow; engine tweens and scripts for UI and camera\",","+    \"audio\": \"All synthesized in code: bluegrass chiptune songs on the engine synth, layered sound effects with valley echoes, ambience beds, Animalese-style gibberish voices\",","+    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 players: the game's own card, a timed 3-minute round, ghost reticles and shots, progress and result reporting\",","+    \"testing\": \"Allowed: unlimited headless testing with the engine's game.advance and game.debug, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, rerun only after changing covered code; screenshots only for what scripts can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\",","+    \"research\": \"Planning stage (2026-11-03): read directly: Wikipedia 'Big Buck Hunter', the Highway Games listing for the Big Buck Hunter Pro cabinet, Macworld's review of the iPhone port; Giant Bomb, TV Tropes, MobyGames and the Sinden wiki refused the fetch (HTTP 403) and a retailer page was rate-limited (HTTP 429), so only search summaries were seen for them; plus the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff docs and the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 docs\",","+    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","+    \"model\": \"unknown\",","+    \"usage\": \"unknown\"","+  },","+  \"testingFeedback\": [","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\"","+  ],","+  \"engineFeedback\": [","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\"","+  ],","+  \"promptFeedback\": [","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\",","+    \"unknown\"","+  ],","+  \"aiHub\": {","+    \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",","+    \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\",","+    \"description\": \"An arcade light-gun hunting shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or online.\",","+    \"type\": \"Game\",","+    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",","+    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",","+    \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",","+    \"players\": \"1–4\",","+    \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call: Q or Triangle\",","+    \"tags\": [","+      \"first-person\",","+      \"arcade\",","+      \"pixel art\",","+      \"versus\",","+      \"comedy\",","+      \"retro\"","+    ]","+  }","+}","+```"," "," ## Appendix F. Research sources","+Read directly:"," - Big Buck Hunter, Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Buck_Hunter","-- Search summaries of: Giant Bomb (Big Buck Hunter Pro), MobyGames (Big Buck Hunter Pro, Wii), Macworld review (iPhone","-  port), Raw Thrills product listing, an achievements list (bonus game names), the Big Buck Hunter Reloaded change log.","-- Engine: my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2 (`README.md`, `API.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, module heade